{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KXEMhcZ5QS2ZDZsqoNt6HR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '原始framing完全成立。31% C%被接受为genuine temporal instability，四条claims按原始强度提出无需hedge。\n2\t  Permutation null (p<0.001)、6-benchmark replication (17.9-31.3%)、ability confound\n3\t  decomposition (2.4pp/7.7%)、 DIF-cleaned demonstration (z=8.5 cohort asymmetry) 构成四重evidence\n4\t  chain。 Systematic confound elimination叙事（architecture=99.98% decoder-only, ability\n5\t  d=-0.17, local independence Q3=0.009, model independence C%≤random at every K, threshold\n6\t  robustness 10-49%, multiple testing BH removes 3/3918） 被视为convincing robustness\n7\t  backbone。Proposition 1 (ΔFPR=0) 和 DIF-cleaned MMLU demonstration 作为双重方法论+实证亮点。10→8页压缩成功，无critical\n8\t  evidence丢失。 Reviewers平均分3.75-4.25，0-2个rebuttal issues，3-4条claims accepted without\n9\t  caveat。\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n14\t  plan_id: plan_001\n15\t  description: 'Apply MH-DIF to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,219 models × 12,508\n16\t    items). Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family\n17\t    confound control, domain-specificity analysis, random-split sanity check.\n18\t\n19\t    '\n20\t  expected_results:\n21\t    temporal_cohort:\n22\t      n_ref: 1080\n23\t      n_foc: 807\n24\t      ets_c_pct: 31.3\n25\t      ets_c_count: 3918\n26\t      ets_b_pct: 23.4\n27\t      ets_a_pct: 45.3\n28\t      bootstrap_ci_95:\n29\t      - 29.5\n30\t      - 33.1\n31\t      bootstrap_n: 1000\n32\t    ability_cohort:\n33\t      ets_c_pct: 2.9\n34\t      enrichment_vs_li: 1.19\n35\t    within_family:\n36\t      llama2_vs_llama3_c_pct: 61.3\n37\t      mistral_vs_mixtral_c_pct: 38.7\n38\t      llama2v3_n_ref: 161\n39\t      llama2v3_n_foc: 308\n40\t    domain_specificity:\n41\t      spearman_rho_dif_vs_acc_improvement: 0.307\n42\t      spearman_p: 0.02\n43\t      n_subjects: 57\n44\t      all_subjects_have_dif: true\n45\t      mean_subject_c_pct: 30.6\n46\t      range_subject_c_pct:\n47\t      - 20.7\n48\t      - 48.4\n49\t    proxy_validation:\n50\t      enrichment_vs_li_temporal: 0.96\n51\t      fpr_on_li_clean: 0.318\n52\t      li_coverage: 0.738\n53\t    sanity:\n54\t      random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n55\t      temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n56\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，31.3% C%被完全接受为genuine temporal instability。理由链： (1) Random\\\n57\t    \\ split sanity check C%=0.18%证明MH procedure本身不inflate false positives； (2) 与Li\\\n58\t    \\ et al. enrichment≈0.96是EXPECTED结果（web-overlap labels测量global exposure而非differential\\\n59\t    \\ contamination），\\n    reviewers接受这是meta-critique的empirical support而非DIF failure；\\n\\\n60\t    (3) Domain correlation ρ=0.307 (p=0.02)表面上暗示ability confound，但plan_019 item-level\\\n61\t    \\ decomposition\\n    将证明domain improvement仅解释2.4pp/7.6%——item-specific instability是dominant\\\n62\t    \\ signal；\\n(4) Within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3%高于temporal 31.3%，说明family-level\\\n63\t    \\ capability gap (d≈-0.99)\\n    确实inflate DIF，但plan_027将证明temporal cohort d=-0.17时confound仅2.4pp；\\n\\\n64\t    (5) 57个subjects全部有DIF (range 20.7-48.4%)证明instability是benchmark-wide现象，非个别subject\\\n65\t    \\ artifact。\\n\"\n66\t  tables:\n67\t  - title: 'Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary — MMLU (5,219 models × 12,508 items)'\n68\t    columns:\n69\t    - Cohort\n70\t    - N_ref\n71\t    - N_foc\n72\t    - ETS_A_pct\n73\t    - ETS_B_pct\n74\t    - ETS_C_pct\n75\t    - Random_C_pct\n76\t    - Enrichment_Li\n77\t    rows:\n78\t    - - Temporal 2023v2024\n79\t      - 1080\n80\t      - 807\n81\t      - 45.3\n82\t      - 23.4\n83\t      - 31.3\n84\t      - 0.18\n85\t      - 0.96\n86\t    - - Ability Q1vQ5\n87\t      - 2608\n88\t      - 2608\n89\t      - 82.1\n90\t      - 15.0\n91\t      - 2.9\n92\t      - 0.15\n93\t      - 1.19\n94\t    - - Within-family Llama2v3\n95\t      - 161\n96\t      - 308\n97\t      - 18.7\n98\t      - 20.0\n99\t      - 61.3\n100\t      - --\n101\t      - --\n102\t  - title: 'Table 2: Domain-Level DIF Distribution (Top/Bottom 5 Subjects)'\n103\t    columns:\n104\t    - Subject\n105\t    - N_items\n106\t    - C_pct\n107\t    - Pct_favor_2024\n108\t    - Domain\n109\t    rows:\n110\t    - - business_ethics\n111\t      - 100\n112\t      - 48.4\n113\t      - 38.0\n114\t      - Social_Science\n115\t    - - human_aging\n116\t      - 223\n117\t      - 41.9\n118\t      - 34.5\n119\t      - Other\n120\t    - - formal_logic\n121\t      - 126\n122\t      - 40.4\n123\t      - 42.1\n124\t      - Humanities\n125\t    - - professional_medicine\n126\t      - 272\n127\t      - 31.1\n128\t      - 51.2\n129\t      - STEM\n130\t    - - high_school_statistics\n131\t      - 216\n132\t      - 42.0\n133\t      - 55.3\n134\t      - STEM\n135\t    - - '...'\n136\t      - --\n137\t      - --\n138\t      - --\n139\t      - --\n140\t    - - computer_security\n141\t      - 100\n142\t      - 20.7\n143\t      - 48.1\n144\t      - STEM\n145\t    - - marketing\n146\t      - 234\n147\t      - 20.9\n148\t      - 40.2\n149\t      - Social_Science\n150\t    - - management\n151\t      - 103\n152\t      - 21.7\n153\t      - 43.7\n154\t      - Social_Science\n155\t  figures_description:\n156\t  - 'Fig 1: Histogram of |Δ_MH| across 12,508 items with ETS A/B/C thresholds annotated.\n157\t    Long right tail shows substantial mass beyond C threshold (|Δ_MH|≥1.5). Random-split\n158\t    overlay (near-zero mass beyond 1.0) as visual contrast.'\n159\t  - 'Fig 2: Subject-level C% heatmap (57 subjects) with domain grouping. Color gradient\n160\t    20-48%. Annotation: domain means (STEM 30.9%, Humanities 31.1%, Social Science\n161\t    31.6%) are statistically indistinguishable (KW p=0.78).'\n162\t  analysis: 'plan_001是整个paper的load-bearing experiment。在best档下，reviewer consensus是：\n163\t    31.3% temporal instability是empirically robust的primary finding（random split 0.18%排除procedural\n164\t    artifact， 6-benchmark replication排除MMLU-specific artifact，permutation null p<0.001排除chance）。\n165\t    Enrichment≈0.96被正确解读为support for Claim 2 (ground truth meta-critique)而非DIF failure。\n166\t    Domain correlation ρ=0.307被acknowleded但item-level decomposition (R²=0.0007)消解了ecological\n167\t    fallacy concern。 Within-family 61.3%被正确contextualized为high-ability-gap scenario\n168\t    (d=-0.99)， 与temporal d=-0.17形成informative contrast。\n169\t\n170\t    '\n171\t- name: rl_robustness_validation\n172\t  plan_id: plan_002\n173\t  description: 'Validate DIF robustness to reasoning-RL models (GRPO/PPO). SFT-only\n174\t    baseline, alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO N=477), and 10-15 reasoning-RL models added to\n175\t    focal cohort. Traditional detectors (Min-K%, ConStat) run on individual RL models.\n176\t\n177\t    '\n178\t  expected_results:\n179\t    sft_baseline:\n180\t      n_models: 312\n181\t      cohort_c_pct: 30.8\n182\t    alignment_rl_cohort:\n183\t      n_models: 477\n184\t      cohort_c_pct: 31.1\n185\t      jaccard_vs_sft_baseline: 0.89\n186\t    reasoning_rl_augmented:\n187\t      n_rl_models_added: 13\n188\t      total_focal_n: 820\n189\t      cohort_c_pct: 31.2\n190\t      jaccard_vs_baseline: 0.94\n191\t      delta_c_pct_vs_no_rl: 0.1\n192\t    traditional_detector_degradation:\n193\t      min_k_auroc_on_sft: 0.72\n194\t      min_k_auroc_on_rl: 0.51\n195\t      constat_auroc_on_sft: 0.68\n196\t      constat_auroc_on_rl: 0.43\n197\t      delong_p_min_k: 0.03\n198\t      delong_p_constat: 0.008\n199\t    power_analysis:\n200\t      detection_boundary_p: 0.45\n201\t      tpr_at_p04_N80_d14: 0.31\n202\t      tpr_at_p07_N80_d14: 0.58\n203\t      tpr_at_p10_N80_d14: 0.68\n204\t    bootstrap_ci_auroc_dif:\n205\t    - 0.88\n206\t    - 0.95\n207\t    tost_equivalence_dif_retention: p=0.02, equivalence margin ±5%\n208\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，N=13 reasoning-RL models被explicitly acknowledged为underpowered（Limitations\\\n209\t    \\ §5）， 但directional evidence仍被视为informative。理由： (1) DIF是group-level method——13个RL\\\n210\t    \\ models混入820个focal cohort后C%仅变化0.1pp，\\n    证明少量RL models不degrade detection（这是method\\\n211\t    \\ property而非sample size claim）；\\n(2) 传统detectors在同一13个模型上AUROC下降21-25个百分点（DeLong\\\n212\t    \\ p<0.05），\\n    提供\\\"DIF robust vs traditional fragile\\\"的directional contrast；\\n\\\n213\t    (3) Partial exploitation power analysis给出formal detection boundary（p≈0.45），\\n\\\n214\t    \\    这是theoretical contribution独立于sample size；\\n(4) Reviewers在best档下接受\\\"theoretically\\\n215\t    \\ motivated + directional empirical support + acknowledged limitation\\\"\\n    的honest\\\n216\t    \\ framing，不要求powered confirmation。\\n关键：paper不claim \\\"DIF is RL-robust\\\" as numbered\\\n217\t    \\ contribution——它出现在systematic confound elimination narrative中作为第5个negative result（reasoning-RL\\\n218\t    \\ doesn't degrade DIF），strength来自pattern （6 confounds tested, all negative）而非individual\\\n219\t    \\ test power。\\n\"\n220\t  tables:\n221\t  - title: 'Table S-RL: DIF Stability Under Cohort Composition Variation'\n222\t    columns:\n223\t    - Cohort_Composition\n224\t    - N_focal\n225\t    - C_pct\n226\t    - Jaccard_vs_Baseline\n227\t    - Delta_C_pp\n228\t    rows:\n229\t    - - SFT-only baseline\n230\t      - 312\n231\t      - 30.8\n232\t      - 1.0\n233\t      - 0.0\n234\t    - - + Alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO)\n235\t      - 477\n236\t      - 31.1\n237\t      - 0.89\n238\t      - 0.3\n239\t    - - + Reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO)\n240\t      - 820\n241\t      - 31.2\n242\t      - 0.94\n243\t      - 0.1\n244\t  - title: 'Table S-RL2: Traditional Detector Degradation on Reasoning-RL Models'\n245\t    columns:\n246\t    - Detector\n247\t    - AUROC_SFT\n248\t    - AUROC_RL\n249\t    - Delta_AUROC\n250\t    - DeLong_p\n251\t    rows:\n252\t    - - Min-K%\n253\t      - 0.72\n254\t      - 0.51\n255\t      - -0.21\n256\t      - 0.03\n257\t    - - ConStat\n258\t      - 0.68\n259\t      - 0.43\n260\t      - -0.25\n261\t      - 0.008\n262\t    - - DIF (group-level)\n263\t      - 0.92\n264\t      - 0.91\n265\t      - -0.01\n266\t      - 0.88\n267\t  figures_description:\n268\t  - 'Fig S-RL: Detection power curve as function of exploitation rate p ∈ [0.4, 1.0]\n269\t    at N=80, δ=1.4. Shaded region shows DIF operational zone (TPR>0.5). Vertical line\n270\t    at p=0.45 marks detection boundary.'\n271\t  analysis: '在best档下，plan_002定位为supplementary evidence in confound elimination narrative，\n272\t    不是standalone claim。Reviewers接受N=13的limitation disclosure，因为： (a) DIF的group-level\n273\t    property在理论上就不依赖于individual RL models的数量； (b) 传统detector对比提供了有意义的contrast； (c)\n274\t    power analysis是theoretical contribution。 如果reviewer提出concern，rebuttal只需指出\"DIF\n275\t    robustness is a group-level property, not a per-model claim — the 13 RL models\n276\t    are added TO a cohort of 820.\"\n277\t\n278\t    '\n279\t- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n280\t  plan_id: plan_003a\n281\t  description: 'Independent evaluation of ConStat-style perturbation testing on 200+\n282\t    MMLU items. LLM paraphrasing → original vs reformulated performance → FDR-controlled\n283\t    detection.\n284\t\n285\t    '\n286\t  expected_results:\n287\t    status: not_executed_future_work\n288\t    in_paper_role: 'ConStat/DVD AUROC numbers and Jaccard overlap with DIF flags cited\n289\t      from literature in main text (§4.2). Direct head-to-head comparison deferred.\n290\t\n291\t      '\n292\t    cited_constat_auroc: 0.62\n293\t    cited_dif_auroc: 0.92\n294\t    jaccard_dif_vs_constat_flags: 0.15\n295\t    rationale_for_low_overlap: 'ConStat detects verbatim memorization (perturbation\n296\t      sensitivity), DIF detects differential functioning across cohorts. Orthogonal\n297\t      signals by construction.\n298\t\n299\t      '\n300\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，plan_003a未执行不构成weakness。理由： (1) Paper已pivot from \\\"ensemble\\\n301\t    \\ detection\\\" to \\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"——ConStat comparison\\n    不是任何numbered\\\n302\t    \\ claim的dependency；\\n(2) Main text已增加ConStat/DVD AUROC numbers和Jaccard overlap\\\n303\t    \\ visibility（Dream #8改进点），\\n    reviewer看到了complementary baselines的positioning；\\n\\\n304\t    (3) Best档reviewers理解\\\"discovery paper, not methods paper\\\"的framing——\\n    head-to-head\\\n305\t    \\ comparison属于future methods work而非本paper scope；\\n(4) Low Jaccard (0.15) 反而support\\\n306\t    \\ meta-critique (Claim 2)：不同detectors捕捉不同signal，\\n    web-overlap ground truth不能simultaneously\\\n307\t    \\ validate all。\\n\"\n308\t  tables: []\n309\t  figures_description: []\n310\t  analysis: 'Not executed. In best tier, acknowledged as complementary baseline in\n311\t    related work, not a missing experiment. ConStat AUROC and Jaccard numbers from\n312\t    literature are sufficient for positioning.\n313\t\n314\t    '\n315\t- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n316\t  plan_id: plan_003b\n317\t  description: 'DVD generation variance evaluation on MMLU. 10-15 open-weight models,\n318\t    50 responses per item via temperature sampling, bimodal distribution detection.\n319\t\n320\t    '\n321\t  expected_results:\n322\t    status: not_executed_future_work\n323\t    in_paper_role: 'DVD cited alongside ConStat as complementary detector in Related\n324\t      Work. Overlap statistics from prior literature referenced in main text.\n325\t\n326\t      '\n327\t    cited_dvd_auroc_variant_contamination: 0.58\n328\t    cited_dvd_auroc_verbatim_contamination: 0.71\n329\t  result_rationale: '与plan_003a同理。DVD evaluation未执行不影响best档outcome。Paper scope是DIF\n330\t    characterization， 不是detector comparison。DVD的generation variance approach检测variant\n331\t    contamination， 与DIF的cohort-differential signal是orthogonal维度。Reviewers在best档下不expecta\n332\t    discovery paper同时实现all possible baselines。\n333\t\n334\t    '\n335\t  tables: []\n336\t  figures_description: []\n337\t  analysis: 'Not executed. DVD is positioned as a complementary approach in Related\n338\t    Work, not as a competing method. Best tier reviewers accept this scope boundary.\n339\t\n340\t    '\n341\t- name: ensemble_fusion\n342\t  plan_id: plan_003c\n343\t  description: 'DIF + ConStat + DVD multi-signal ensemble with calibrated thresholds,\n344\t    majority voting, weighted fusion. Depends on plan_003a and plan_003b.\n345\t\n346\t    '\n347\t  expected_results:\n348\t    status: dropped_dependencies_not_met\n349\t    in_paper_role: Acknowledged as future direction in §5 Discussion.\n350\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，ensemble fusion被clean地dropped为future work。理由： (1) Paper已从\\\"\\\n351\t    detection ensemble\\\"完全pivot到\\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"——\\n    ensemble不是any claim的dependency；\\n\\\n352\t    (2) Dependencies (plan_003a/b) 未执行，cascade drop是logical； (3) Best档reviewers不会要求discovery\\\n353\t    \\ paper同时deliver a detection system； (4) §5 Discussion中\\\"future work: ensemble\\\n354\t    \\ combining DIF's cohort-level signal with\\n    ConStat's perturbation signal\\\n355\t    \\ and DVD's generation variance\\\"被视为reasonable next step。\\n\"\n356\t  tables: []\n357\t  figures_description: []\n358\t  analysis: 'Cleanly dropped. Ensemble was part of original \"detection paper\" framing;\n359\t    pivot to \"characterization paper\" removes it from scope. No reviewer concern in\n360\t    best tier.\n361\t\n362\t    '\n363\t- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n364\t  plan_id: plan_004\n365\t  description: 'Replicate DIF on GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models) with GSM1K contamination\n366\t    gap as independent ground truth. Semi-synthetic validation. Temporal DIF replication.\n367\t\n368\t    '\n369\t  expected_results:\n370\t    step1_temporal_dif:\n371\t      n_items: 1319\n372\t      n_ref: 1017\n373\t      n_foc: 804\n374\t      standard_c_pct: 18.9\n375\t      external_c_pct: 47.4\n376\t      sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n377\t      standard_external_spearman: 0.926\n378\t    step2_semi_synthetic:\n379\t      standard_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n380\t      external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.517\n381\t      standard_delta_fpr: 0.0\n382\t      external_delta_fpr: 0.0\n383\t    step3_gsm1k_correlation:\n384\t      n_models: 33\n385\t      pearson_r: -0.478\n386\t      pearson_p: 0.005\n387\t      spearman_rho: -0.403\n388\t      spearman_p: 0.02\n389\t      partial_r_controlling_accuracy: -0.385\n390\t      partial_p: 0.027\n391\t      permutation_p: 0.014\n392\t      direction: NEGATIVE — opposite to simple contamination hypothesis\n393\t      cook_d_max_model: Deepseek-math-7b-rl\n394\t      leave_one_out_r_range:\n395\t      - -0.537\n396\t      - -0.374\n397\t      robust: true\n398\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，GSM8K results serve三重purpose： (1) C%=18.9%确认temporal\\\n399\t    \\ DIF不是MMLU-specific（plan_028将extend到6 benchmarks）； (2) Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=+0.818证明framework\\\n400\t    \\ portability到single-domain benchmark\\n    （甚至比MMLU的+0.674更高，因为GSM8K是单一domain，matching更clean）；\\n\\\n401\t    (3) GSM1K anti-correlation r=-0.478被DEMOTED to exploratory（N=33, CI wide [-0.71,\\\n402\t    \\ -0.16]）——\\n    best档reviewers接受这个honest demotion，视为\\\"suggestive but not conclusive\\\"\\\n403\t    。\\nAnti-correlation方向（DIF flags items where 2024 models do WORSE relative to ability，\\\n404\t    \\ 与simple contamination hypothesis相反）在best档下被interpret为DIF捕捉\\\"genuine item functioning\\\n405\t    \\ changes\\\" 而非contamination signal——这SUPPORTS pivot from detection to characterization。\\\n406\t    \\ Robust to outlier removal (leave-one-out range stable) 消解cherry-picking concern。\\n\"\n407\t  tables:\n408\t  - title: 'Table 3: Cross-Benchmark DIF Replication — GSM8K'\n409\t    columns:\n410\t    - Analysis\n411\t    - Metric\n412\t    - Value\n413\t    rows:\n414\t    - - Temporal DIF\n415\t      - C%\n416\t      - 18.9\n417\t    - - Temporal DIF\n418\t      - Random control C%\n419\t      - 0.3\n420\t    - - Semi-synthetic\n421\t      - ΔTPR (p=1.0)\n422\t      - 0.818\n423\t    - - Semi-synthetic\n424\t      - ΔFPR\n425\t      - 0.0\n426\t    - - GSM1K correlation\n427\t      - Pearson r\n428\t      - -0.478 (p=0.005)\n429\t    - - GSM1K correlation\n430\t      - N models\n431\t      - 33\n432\t  figures_description:\n433\t  - 'Fig S-GSM: GSM8K-GSM1K accuracy gap vs DIF-C item fraction (N=33 models). Negative\n434\t    correlation with 95% CI band. Annotated: Deepseek-math-7b-rl as highest Cook''s\n435\t    D point.'\n436\t  analysis: 'GSM8K replication是Claim 3 (framework portability)的primary evidence和Claim\n437\t    4的exploratory support。 在best档下，ΔTPR=+0.818被视为strong validation of semi-synthetic\n438\t    framework。 GSM1K anti-correlation的honest demotion to exploratory被视为intellectual\n439\t    honesty signal， strengthening reviewer trust in the paper''s overall claims.\n440\t\n441\t    '\n442\t- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n443\t  plan_id: plan_005\n444\t  description: 'Fit bifactor model (general + 57 subject-specific factors) to MMLU.\n445\t    Select anchor items, fixed-parameter calibration for replacement items.\n446\t\n447\t    '\n448\t  expected_results:\n449\t    status: killed\n450\t    reason: 'Bifactor model fit insufficient for MMLU''s 57-subject structure. Within-subject\n451\t      DIF (plan_014) showed C%=38.1% — even after controlling for subject-specific\n452\t      ability, DIF remains high. Bifactor equating requires well-fitting measurement\n453\t      model as prerequisite; MMLU''s inherent multidimensionality (57 heterogeneous\n454\t      subjects) prevents adequate fit.\n455\t\n456\t      '\n457\t    attempted_fit_metrics:\n458\t      rmsea: '>0.08 (poor)'\n459\t      cfi: <0.90 (poor)\n460\t      convergence: partial — general factor loadings unstable for small subjects\n461\t    implication: 'Regeneration/equating approach (original Claim 3) killed. Pivot:\n462\t      DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter.\n463\t\n464\t      '\n465\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，bifactor failure被reframed为informative negative result\\\n466\t    \\ in the systematic confound elimination narrative。理由： (1) Bifactor failure demonstrates\\\n467\t    \\ MMLU的inherent multidimensionality——这motivates\\n    \\\"1D IRT is fundamentally\\\n468\t    \\ misspecified for MMLU\\\" limitation disclosure；\\n(2) 这个negative result SUPPORTS\\\n469\t    \\ current framing：如果bifactor worked，paper就会走\\n    equating/regeneration路线；bifactor\\\n470\t    \\ failure推动了更有insight的\\\"diagnostic lens\\\" pivot；\\n(3) Best档reviewers视pivot from\\\n471\t    \\ regeneration to characterization为intellectual maturity，\\n    不是failure；\\n(4)\\\n472\t    \\ Limitations §5中\\\"future multidimensional IRT work\\\"被视为honest acknowledgment\\\n473\t    \\ of scope。\\n\"\n474\t  tables: []\n475\t  figures_description: []\n476\t  analysis: 'Killed experiment. In best tier, this is part of the \"honest science\"\n477\t    narrative: we tried equating, it didn''t work for MMLU, so we pivoted to the more\n478\t    appropriate diagnostic framing. Reviewers appreciate the transparency.\n479\t\n480\t    '\n481\t- name: item_generation_calibration\n482\t  plan_id: plan_006\n483\t  description: 'Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM\n484\t    generation with construct constraints, calibrated via student simulation.\n485\t\n486\t    '\n487\t  expected_results:\n488\t    status: blocked_dependency_killed\n489\t    reason: 'Depends on plan_005 (bifactor equating) which was killed. Without a well-fitting\n490\t      measurement model, replacement item calibration lacks the psychometric foundation\n491\t      for equated score equivalence.\n492\t\n493\t      '\n494\t    preliminary_findings_if_attempted:\n495\t      prompt_difficulty_correlation: 0.15-0.25\n496\t      simulation_difficulty_correlation: 0.75-0.82\n497\t      gap: 'Even with good difficulty estimation, without bifactor equating, replaced\n498\t        benchmark scores are not psychometrically comparable.\n499\t\n500\t        '\n501\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，plan_006 blocked是logical cascade from plan_005 failure。\n502\t    Paper已pivot away from \"replace bad items\"到\"understand what changed\"—— item generation不在current\n503\t    scope内。Reviewers不expect characterization paper 同时deliver item generation pipeline。§5\n504\t    Discussion中brief mention of \"future: automated item generation calibrated via\n505\t    student simulation\" suffices。\n506\t\n507\t    '\n508\t  tables: []\n509\t  figures_description: []\n510\t  analysis: 'Blocked by dependency. In best tier, this is cleanly out of scope for\n511\t    a characterization/discovery paper. Future work mention in Discussion is sufficient.\n512\t\n513\t    '\n514\t- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n515\t  plan_id: plan_007\n516\t  description: 'Simulate cumulative Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006) across\n517\t    4 successive benchmark administrations. Show power accumulation.\n518\t\n519\t    '\n520\t  expected_results:\n521\t    simulation_design:\n522\t      n_administrations: 4\n523\t      items_per_admin: 500\n524\t      n_ref_per_admin: 200\n525\t      n_foc_per_admin: 200\n526\t      delta_range:\n527\t      - 0.8\n528\t      - 1.6\n529\t      prior: non-informative → informative (accumulated evidence)\n530\t    power_trajectory:\n531\t      admin_1_tpr_d10: 0.4\n532\t      admin_2_tpr_d10: 0.55\n533\t      admin_3_tpr_d10: 0.7\n534\t      admin_4_tpr_d10: 0.78\n535\t      admin_1_tpr_d14: 0.68\n536\t      admin_2_tpr_d14: 0.8\n537\t      admin_3_tpr_d14: 0.88\n538\t      admin_4_tpr_d14: 0.93\n539\t    fpr_all_administrations:\n540\t    - 0.042\n541\t    - 0.044\n542\t    - 0.043\n543\t    - 0.045\n544\t    bayes_factor_accumulation:\n545\t      admin_1_median_bf: 3.2\n546\t      admin_3_median_bf: 28.5\n547\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，cumulative Bayesian DIF是appendix-level simulation showing\\\n548\t    \\ practical potential for longitudinal benchmark monitoring。理由： (1) Power从0.40→0.70\\\n549\t    \\ (δ=1.0) across 3 administrations demonstrate evidence accumulation的value——\\n\\\n550\t    \\    这address \\\"MH needs large effects\\\" concern by showing medium effects become\\\n551\t    \\ detectable over time；\\n(2) FPR保持stable (<0.05) across administrations证明prior\\\n552\t    \\ accumulation不inflate false positives； (3) 这是audit protocol (Claim 4) 的technical\\\n553\t    \\ foundation：\\\"monitor quarterly, accumulate DIF evidence\\\"； (4) Simulation-only\\\n554\t    \\ status被accept因为这是methodological suggestion for future adoption，\\n    不是empirical\\\n555\t    \\ claim。\\nBest档reviewer视为\\\"nice-to-have appendix that shows the authors thought\\\n556\t    \\ about practical deployment\\\"。\\n\"\n557\t  tables:\n558\t  - title: 'Table S-Bayes: Cumulative DIF Power Across Administrations'\n559\t    columns:\n560\t    - Admin\n561\t    - N_accumulated\n562\t    - TPR_d08\n563\t    - TPR_d10\n564\t    - TPR_d14\n565\t    - FPR\n566\t    rows:\n567\t    - - 1\n568\t      - 400\n569\t      - 0.22\n570\t      - 0.4\n571\t      - 0.68\n572\t      - 0.042\n573\t    - - 2\n574\t      - 800\n575\t      - 0.35\n576\t      - 0.55\n577\t      - 0.8\n578\t      - 0.044\n579\t    - - 3\n580\t      - 1200\n581\t      - 0.5\n582\t      - 0.7\n583\t      - 0.88\n584\t      - 0.043\n585\t    - - 4\n586\t      - 1600\n587\t      - 0.59\n588\t      - 0.78\n589\t      - 0.93\n590\t      - 0.045\n591\t  figures_description:\n592\t  - 'Fig S-Bayes: Power accumulation curves (TPR vs administration number) at δ={0.8,\n593\t    1.0, 1.4, 1.6}. Horizontal dashed line at TPR=0.80 (conventional adequate power).\n594\t    Shows medium effects crossing 0.80 by admin 2-3.'\n595\t  analysis: 'Appendix simulation. In best tier, reviewers appreciate the forward-looking\n596\t    methodological contribution. Key insight: medium DIF effects (δ=1.0, currently\n597\t    TPR=0.40) become reliably detectable with 3 administrations — this makes the audit\n598\t    protocol in Claim 4 practically viable.\n599\t\n600\t    '\n601\t- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n602\t  plan_id: plan_008\n603\t  description: 'Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement/removal.\n604\t    Ranking stability, score reliability, construct coverage as function of replacement\n605\t    rate.\n606\t\n607\t    '\n608\t  expected_results:\n609\t    progressive_removal:\n610\t      pct_5_rho: 0.9998\n611\t      pct_10_rho: 0.9993\n612\t      pct_20_rho: 0.9976\n613\t      pct_31_rho: 0.9965\n614\t      pct_50_rho: 0.9891\n615\t    reliability_cronbach_alpha:\n616\t      full_12508: 0.994\n617\t      minus_5pct: 0.993\n618\t      minus_10pct: 0.993\n619\t      minus_20pct: 0.991\n620\t      minus_31pct: 0.99\n621\t      minus_50pct: 0.985\n622\t    construct_coverage:\n623\t      subjects_losing_gt10pct_items_at_31pct_removal: 4\n624\t      min_items_per_subject_after_31pct: 42\n625\t      coverage_ratio_at_31pct: 0.96\n626\t    theoretical_bound: 'For r-item removal from N-item benchmark with uniform discrimination,\n627\t      ranking stability ≥ 1 - (r/N)² when items are randomly sampled. DIF-targeted\n628\t      removal is slightly more disruptive than random (z=-9.5 vs random expectation),\n629\t      but well within the theoretical bound.\n630\t\n631\t      '\n632\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，graceful degradation analysis直接support \\\"instability\\\n633\t    \\ ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative： (1) ρ=0.9965 at 31% removal证明MMLU has massive measurement\\\n634\t    \\ redundancy——\\n    removing 3,918 items barely changes rankings；\\n(2) Cronbach\\\n635\t    \\ α从0.994降到0.990说明reliability几乎不受影响； (3) Construct coverage 96%说明所有subjects仍有adequate\\\n636\t    \\ item representation； (4) Theoretical bound给出formal explanation：with 12,508 items,\\\n637\t    \\ removing 31%\\n    (≈3,900 items) 只损失(0.31)²≈9.6% of ranking precision，而actual\\\n638\t    \\ degradation\\n    更小因为DIF items are moderate-discrimination (d=0.230 above average但不extreme)；\\n\\\n639\t    (5) 这个result是plan_017 (downstream impact) 的complementary angle——\\n    plan_017\\\n640\t    \\ shows DIF removal is MORE disruptive than random (signal存在),\\n    plan_008 shows\\\n641\t    \\ even this \\\"more disruptive\\\" is still tiny (magnitude小)。\\n\"\n642\t  tables:\n643\t  - title: 'Table S-Degrade: Benchmark Validity Under Progressive Item Removal'\n644\t    columns:\n645\t    - Pct_Removed\n646\t    - N_Remaining\n647\t    - Spearman_rho\n648\t    - Cronbach_alpha\n649\t    - Coverage_ratio\n650\t    rows:\n651\t    - - 5\n652\t      - 11883\n653\t      - 0.9998\n654\t      - 0.993\n655\t      - 0.99\n656\t    - - 10\n657\t      - 11257\n658\t      - 0.9993\n659\t      - 0.993\n660\t      - 0.98\n661\t    - - 20\n662\t      - 10006\n663\t      - 0.9976\n664\t      - 0.991\n665\t      - 0.97\n666\t    - - 31 (DIF-C)\n667\t      - 8590\n668\t      - 0.9965\n669\t      - 0.99\n670\t      - 0.96\n671\t    - - 50\n672\t      - 6254\n673\t      - 0.9891\n674\t      - 0.985\n675\t      - 0.91\n676\t  figures_description:\n677\t  - 'Fig S-Degrade: Spearman ρ vs percentage of items removed. Two curves: random\n678\t    removal (smooth decline) and DIF-targeted removal (slightly steeper but still\n679\t    >0.99 at 31%). Shaded region between curves shows DIF excess disruption.'\n680\t  analysis: 'Appendix result. In best tier, this provides the quantitative backbone\n681\t    for \"instability ≠ invalidity\" — reviewers can see that 31% item instability translates\n682\t    to <0.4% ranking disruption (1-0.9965). The redundancy finding is itself noteworthy:\n683\t    MMLU could lose a third of its items with negligible impact on model comparison.\n684\t\n685\t    '\n686\t- name: item_focused_trees\n687\t  plan_id: plan_009\n688\t  description: 'Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) with continuous release-date\n689\t    covariate. Alternative to categorical temporal DIF. Avoids arbitrary cohort split.\n690\t\n691\t    '\n692\t  expected_results:\n693\t    n_items_analyzed: 12508\n694\t    n_models: 5219\n695\t    tree_depth_median: 3\n696\t    tree_split_dates:\n697\t      most_common_first_split: 2023-09 to 2023-11\n698\t      second_split_range: 2024-03 to 2024-05\n699\t    ift_dif_detection_rate: 33.8\n700\t    concordance_with_mh_c:\n701\t      jaccard: 0.78\n702\t      kappa: 0.74\n703\t      mh_only_pct: 5.2\n704\t      ift_only_pct: 7.7\n705\t    temporal_gradient:\n706\t      dif_magnitude_increases_with_time: true\n707\t      linear_slope_delta_mh_per_month: 0.08\n708\t      nonlinear_detected: true\n709\t      inflection_point: 2023-Q4\n710\t    advantage_over_categorical: 'IFT reveals that DIF onset concentrates in 2023-Q4,\n711\t      suggesting a temporal boundary related to training data cutoff shifts.\n712\t\n713\t      '\n714\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，IFT analysis是appendix robustness check confirming两个key\\\n715\t    \\ findings： (1) Jaccard=0.78 with MH-DIF说明categorical split (2023 vs 2024)捕捉了most\\\n716\t    \\ of the signal——\\n    MH's simplicity是justified；\\n(2) IFT发现DIF onset集中在2023-Q4（inflection\\\n717\t    \\ point），这对应于GPT-4/Claude-2.1等\\n    major model releases时期，提供temporal DIF的concrete\\\n718\t    \\ interpretation；\\n(3) C%=33.8% vs MH's 31.3%说明continuous approach捕捉slightly more\\\n719\t    \\ DIF\\n    （expected：避免了arbitrary split的information loss），但差异modest；\\n(4) Nonlinear\\\n720\t    \\ temporal gradient证明DIF不是simple linear drift而是有specific onset period，\\n    这支持\\\"\\\n721\t    training data vintage drives item functioning changes\\\" interpretation。\\nBest档reviewer视为\\\"\\\n722\t    nice robustness check that adds interpretive value\\\"。\\n\"\n723\t  tables:\n724\t  - title: 'Table S-IFT: Item-Focused Trees vs Categorical MH-DIF'\n725\t    columns:\n726\t    - Metric\n727\t    - MH-DIF\n728\t    - IFT\n729\t    - Agreement\n730\t    rows:\n731\t    - - Detection rate\n732\t      - 31.3%\n733\t      - 33.8%\n734\t      - Jaccard=0.78\n735\t    - - FPR (random split)\n736\t      - 0.18%\n737\t      - 0.22%\n738\t      - --\n739\t    - - Temporal resolution\n740\t      - Binary 2023/2024\n741\t      - Continuous release date\n742\t      - --\n743\t  figures_description:\n744\t  - 'Fig S-IFT: DIF magnitude (mean |Δ_MH| equivalent) vs model release month. Scatter\n745\t    with LOESS smoother. Vertical line at 2023-Q4 inflection point. Shows DIF onset\n746\t    concentration.'\n747\t  analysis: 'Appendix robustness. In best tier, IFT confirms MH findings while adding\n748\t    temporal granularity. The 2023-Q4 inflection finding is interpretively valuable\n749\t    but kept in appendix to avoid overloading the main narrative.\n750\t\n751\t    '\n752\t- name: architecture_stratified_dif\n753\t  plan_id: plan_010\n754\t  description: 'DIF within decoder-only subpopulation. Test whether architecture heterogeneity\n755\t    drives spurious DIF. IRT fit diagnostics on homogeneous subgroup.\n756\t\n757\t    '\n758\t  expected_results:\n759\t    architecture_composition:\n760\t      total_models: 5227\n761\t      decoder_only: 5226\n762\t      non_decoder: 1\n763\t      pct_decoder_only: 99.98\n764\t    decoder_only_dif:\n765\t      c_pct: 31.3\n766\t      jaccard_vs_full: 1.0\n767\t      n_items_changed: 0\n768\t    irt_fit:\n769\t      rmsea_full: 0.082\n770\t      rmsea_decoder_only: 0.082\n771\t      note: IRT fit unchanged — misfit is due to MMLU multidimensionality (57 subjects),\n772\t        not architecture\n773\t    conclusion: Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue for METABENCH MMLU\n774\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，这是confound elimination narrative中最clean的negative result。理由：\\\n775\t    \\ (1) METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227)——removing 1 non-decoder\\\n776\t    \\ model\\n    changes literally nothing (Jaccard=1.0, 0 items change classification)；\\n\\\n777\t    (2) IRT fit不improve because misfit来自MMLU's 57-subject multidimensionality，\\n \\\n778\t    \\   不是architecture heterogeneity——这被explicitly discussed in Limitations；\\n(3)\\\n779\t    \\ 这个result turns potential reviewer concern into a non-issue in one sentence：\\n\\\n780\t    \\    \\\"METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only; architecture stratification changes\\\n781\t    \\ zero items.\\\"\\nBest档reviewer看到这个数字后不会再raise architecture concern。 这是systematic\\\n782\t    \\ confound elimination的第1个pillar（architecture → ability → local dependence → IRT\\\n783\t    \\ misfit → model independence → reasoning-RL）。\\n\"\n784\t  tables:\n785\t  - title: 'Table S-Arch: Architecture Composition and DIF Impact'\n786\t    columns:\n787\t    - Subpopulation\n788\t    - N_models\n789\t    - C_pct\n790\t    - Jaccard_vs_Full\n791\t    rows:\n792\t    - - Full population\n793\t      - 5227\n794\t      - 31.3\n795\t      - 1.0\n796\t    - - Decoder-only\n797\t      - 5226\n798\t      - 31.3\n799\t      - 1.0\n800\t    - - Non-decoder (encoder-decoder)\n801\t      - 1\n802\t      - --\n803\t      - --\n804\t  figures_description: []\n805\t  analysis: 'Cleanest possible confound elimination: 99.98% homogeneity means architecture\n806\t    stratification is a one-line defense. In best tier, this is cited in §4.1 as first\n807\t    robustness check and never questioned again.\n808\t\n809\t    '\n810\t- name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n811\t  plan_id: plan_011\n812\t  description: 'Inject known contamination into real METABENCH response matrix. Measure\n813\t    DIF TPR/FPR under controlled ground truth. Vary exploitation rate p ∈ [0.3, 1.0].\n814\t\n815\t    '\n816\t  expected_results:\n817\t    temporal_external_matching:\n818\t      baseline_fpr: 0.314\n819\t      tpr_p00: 0.326\n820\t      tpr_p03: 0.548\n821\t      tpr_p05: 0.834\n822\t      tpr_p07: 0.99\n823\t      tpr_p10: 1.0\n824\t      delta_tpr_p05: 0.508\n825\t      delta_tpr_p10: 0.674\n826\t      fpr_stable_across_p: true\n827\t      fpr_at_p10: 0.314\n828\t    cross_subject_matching:\n829\t      delta_fpr_all_subjects: 0.0\n830\t      delta_tpr_p05_mean: 0.347\n831\t      subjects_passing_p05: 4/5\n832\t      proposition_1_confirmed: true\n833\t    within_subject_matching:\n834\t      fpr_inflation_at_p10: 0.186\n835\t      matching_variable_contamination: true\n836\t    dose_response:\n837\t      monotonic: true\n838\t      inflection_p: 0.35\n839\t      saturation_p: 0.7\n840\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，semi-synthetic validation是Claim 3的primary evidence。理由：\\\n841\t    \\ (1) ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5证明DIF can detect moderate differential contamination\\n\\\n842\t    \\    in real response matrices——这不是simulation，是real data + controlled injection；\\n\\\n843\t    (2) Cross-subject matching ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 subjects是Proposition 1的empirical证明——\\n\\\n844\t    \\    using total score on OTHER subjects as matching variable完全eliminates FPR\\\n845\t    \\ inflation；\\n(3) Within-subject matching的FPR inflation (+0.186)提供informative\\\n846\t    \\ contrast：\\n    matching variable contamination是real problem，cross-subject matching是real\\\n847\t    \\ solution；\\n(4) Dose-response从p=0.3到p=1.0的monotonic curve证明detection power scales\\\n848\t    \\ with\\n    contamination intensity——不是all-or-nothing；\\n(5) Baseline FPR=0.314\\\n849\t    \\ (close to temporal C%=31.3%)说明semi-synthetic preserves\\n    real DIF structure——injection\\\n850\t    \\ adds TO existing DIF rather than replacing it。\\nReviewer在best档下视Proposition\\\n851\t    \\ 1 (ΔFPR=0)为methodological novelty contribution。\\n\"\n852\t  tables:\n853\t  - title: 'Table 4: Semi-Synthetic Validation — ΔTPR and ΔFPR by Matching Strategy'\n854\t    columns:\n855\t    - Matching\n856\t    - ΔFPR\n857\t    - ΔTPR_p03\n858\t    - ΔTPR_p05\n859\t    - ΔTPR_p10\n860\t    rows:\n861\t    - - Cross-subject (external)\n862\t      - 0.0\n863\t      - 0.222\n864\t      - 0.508\n865\t      - 0.674\n866\t    - - Within-subject (standard)\n867\t      - 0.186\n868\t      - 0.134\n869\t      - 0.298\n870\t      - 0.302\n871\t    - - Cross-benchmark (GSM8K)\n872\t      - 0.0\n873\t      - --\n874\t      - --\n875\t      - 0.818\n876\t  figures_description:\n877\t  - 'Fig 3: Dose-response curve — ΔTPR vs exploitation rate p. Cross-subject matching\n878\t    (blue, ΔFPR=0) vs within-subject (red, FPR inflates). Vertical dashed at p=0.5.\n879\t    Shows cross-subject dominance across entire range.'\n880\t  - 'Fig 4: Proposition 1 illustration — FPR remains constant at all injection levels\n881\t    under cross-subject matching. 5-panel (one per subject) showing FPR flatline vs\n882\t    within-subject inflation.'\n883\t  analysis: 'Load-bearing for Claim 3. In best tier, Proposition 1 (ΔFPR=0) is viewed\n884\t    as the paper''s most elegant methodological contribution: a simple, principled\n885\t    solution to matching variable contamination with an algebraic proof and empirical\n886\t    confirmation across 5 subjects and 2 benchmarks. The dose-response curve provides\n887\t    the operational characterization.\n888\t\n889\t    '\n890\t- name: multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\n891\t  plan_id: plan_028\n892\t  description: 'Temporal DIF on 6 benchmarks: MMLU, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag, WinoGrande,\n893\t    TruthfulQA, GSM8K. All from METABENCH.\n894\t\n895\t    '\n896\t  expected_results:\n897\t    benchmarks:\n898\t      mmlu:\n899\t        n_items: 12508\n900\t        n_ref: 1080\n901\t        n_foc: 807\n902\t        c_pct: 31.3\n903\t        random_c_pct: 0.18\n904\t        bootstrap_ci:\n905\t        - 29.4\n906\t        - 38.1\n907\t      winogrande:\n908\t        n_items: 1267\n909\t        n_ref: 1017\n910\t        n_foc: 803\n911\t        c_pct: 30.3\n912\t        random_c_pct: 0.32\n913\t      truthfulqa:\n914\t        n_items: 817\n915\t        n_ref: 1080\n916\t        n_foc: 807\n917\t        c_pct: 29.7\n918\t        random_c_pct: 0.37\n919\t      arc:\n920\t        n_items: 1172\n921\t        n_ref: 1080\n922\t        n_foc: 807\n923\t        c_pct: 26.9\n924\t        random_c_pct: 0.6\n925\t      gsm8k:\n926\t        n_items: 1319\n927\t        n_ref: 1017\n928\t        n_foc: 804\n929\t        c_pct: 18.9\n930\t        random_c_pct: 0.3\n931\t      hellaswag:\n932\t        n_items: 10042\n933\t        n_ref: 1080\n934\t        n_foc: 807\n935\t        c_pct: 17.9\n936\t        random_c_pct: 0.28\n937\t    cross_benchmark_summary:\n938\t      range_c_pct: 17.9-31.3%\n939\t      all_random_below_1pct: true\n940\t      min_enrichment_ratio: 45\n941\t      n_benchmarks: 6\n942\t      mean_c_pct: 25.8\n943\t      median_c_pct: 28.3\n944\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，6-benchmark replication是generalizability claim的decisive\\\n945\t    \\ evidence。理由： (1) 所有6个benchmarks显示substantial temporal DIF (17.9-31.3%)，远超random\\\n946\t    \\ controls (<1%)； (2) Enrichment ratio ≥45×排除statistical artifact across all benchmarks；\\\n947\t    \\ (3) Range 17.9-31.3%显示benchmark-specific variation但consistent phenomenon——\\n\\\n948\t    \\    knowledge-intensive benchmarks (MMLU 31.3%, TruthfulQA 29.7%) 高于\\n    reasoning\\\n949\t    \\ benchmarks (GSM8K 18.9%, HellaSwag 17.9%)，这是interpretable pattern；\\n(4) 6 benchmarks\\\n950\t    \\ × random controls × consistent pattern构成overwhelming evidence\\n    for temporal\\\n951\t    \\ DIF as general benchmark phenomenon而非MMLU artifact；\\n(5) Best档reviewers视6-benchmark\\\n952\t    \\ consistency为paper的strongest empirical argument之一。 这直接address Dream #6的\\\"only\\\n953\t    \\ MMLU + GSM8K, generalizability insufficient\\\" concern。\\n\"\n954\t  tables:\n955\t  - title: 'Table 5: Temporal DIF Across 6 Benchmarks'\n956\t    columns:\n957\t    - Benchmark\n958\t    - N_items\n959\t    - N_ref\n960\t    - N_foc\n961\t    - C_pct\n962\t    - Random_C_pct\n963\t    - Enrichment\n964\t    rows:\n965\t    - - MMLU\n966\t      - 12508\n967\t      - 1080\n968\t      - 807\n969\t      - 31.3\n970\t      - 0.18\n971\t      - 174×\n972\t    - - WinoGrande\n973\t      - 1267\n974\t      - 1017\n975\t      - 803\n976\t      - 30.3\n977\t      - 0.32\n978\t      - 95×\n979\t    - - TruthfulQA\n980\t      - 817\n981\t      - 1080\n982\t      - 807\n983\t      - 29.7\n984\t      - 0.37\n985\t      - 80×\n986\t    - - ARC-Challenge\n987\t      - 1172\n988\t      - 1080\n989\t      - 807\n990\t      - 26.9\n991\t      - 0.6\n992\t      - 45×\n993\t    - - GSM8K\n994\t      - 1319\n995\t      - 1017\n996\t      - 804\n997\t      - 18.9\n998\t      - 0.3\n999\t      - 63×\n1000\t    - - HellaSwag\n1001\t      - 10042\n1002\t      - 1080\n1003\t      - 807\n1004\t      - 17.9\n1005\t      - 0.28\n1006\t      - 64×\n1007\t  figures_description:\n1008\t  - 'Fig 5: Bar chart of C% across 6 benchmarks (descending) with random control overlay\n1009\t    (<1% barely visible). Error bars from bootstrap CI. Demonstrates generalizability\n1010\t    of temporal DIF phenomenon.'\n1011\t  analysis: 'Load-bearing for generalizability. In best tier, 6-benchmark consistency\n1012\t    is the single strongest defense against \"MMLU-specific artifact\" reviewer concern.\n1013\t    The knowledge-intensive > reasoning pattern adds interpretive value.\n1014\t\n1015\t    '\n1016\t- name: permutation_null_c_rate\n1017\t  plan_id: plan_029\n1018\t  description: '1000× permutation test: randomly reassign 2023/2024 labels (preserving\n1019\t    N_ref=1080, N_foc=807), run MH-DIF each time. Establish null distribution for\n1020\t    C%.\n1021\t\n1022\t    '\n1023\t  expected_results:\n1024\t    n_permutations: 1000\n1025\t    null_distribution:\n1026\t      mean_c_pct: 0.22\n1027\t      sd_c_pct: 0.05\n1028\t      max_c_pct: 0.41\n1029\t      min_c_pct: 0.08\n1030\t      q95_c_pct: 0.31\n1031\t      q99_c_pct: 0.36\n1032\t    observed_c_pct: 31.3\n1033\t    z_score: 622.0\n1034\t    p_value: <0.001 (observed never reached in 1000 permutations)\n1035\t    enrichment_vs_null_mean: 142.3\n1036\t    null_shape: approximately normal, centered near random-split control\n1037\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，permutation null是\\\"is 31% above chance?\\\"的definitive\\\n1038\t    \\ answer。理由： (1) Null mean C%=0.22%几乎identical to within-cohort random split C%=0.18%——\\n\\\n1039\t    \\    这validates random split as adequate null proxy，同时提供formal permutation-based\\\n1040\t    \\ confirmation；\\n(2) Observed 31.3% never appears in 1000 permutations (max null=0.41%)——\\n\\\n1041\t    \\    z=622是absurdly significant，p<0.001 is conservative understatement；\\n(3) Null\\\n1042\t    \\ distribution shape (normal, sd=0.05%) shows temporal label assignment\\n    matters\\\n1043\t    \\ enormously——C% drops 150× when temporal structure is destroyed；\\n(4) 这消除last\\\n1044\t    \\ remaining \\\"statistical artifact\\\" concern：31% is not chance，\\n    not multiple\\\n1045\t    \\ testing artifact (BH removes 3/3918), not procedural artifact\\n    (random split\\\n1046\t    \\ 0.18%), and not temporal label artifact (permutation null 0.22%)；\\n(5) Best档reviewers视permutation\\\n1047\t    \\ test为gold-standard significance evidence，\\n    与bootstrap CI (29.5-33.1%)一起provide\\\n1048\t    \\ complete uncertainty quantification。\\n关键insight：null mean (0.22%)和random split\\\n1049\t    \\ (0.18%)的consistency说明MH procedure itself has near-zero false positive rate——observed\\\n1050\t    \\ C% is almost entirely signal。\\n\"\n1051\t  tables:\n1052\t  - title: 'Table 6: Permutation Null Distribution vs Observed C%'\n1053\t    columns:\n1054\t    - Statistic\n1055\t    - Value\n1056\t    rows:\n1057\t    - - Observed C%\n1058\t      - 31.3\n1059\t    - - Permutation null mean\n1060\t      - 0.22\n1061\t    - - Permutation null SD\n1062\t      - 0.05\n1063\t    - - Permutation null max (N=1000)\n1064\t      - 0.41\n1065\t    - - z-score\n1066\t      - 622.0\n1067\t    - - p-value\n1068\t      - <0.001\n1069\t    - - Random-split control (within-cohort)\n1070\t      - 0.18\n1071\t  figures_description:\n1072\t  - 'Fig 6: Permutation null distribution (histogram, 1000 draws) centered at 0.22%\n1073\t    with observed 31.3% as vertical red line far off the right edge. Inset: zoomed\n1074\t    view of null distribution showing tight concentration around 0.2%. Visual demonstrates\n1075\t    observed C% is not remotely consistent with null.'\n1076\t  analysis: 'Load-bearing for statistical credibility. In best tier, the permutation\n1077\t    test is the capstone of the \"not an artifact\" argument chain. z=622 is so extreme\n1078\t    that no reviewer can question statistical significance. Combined with bootstrap\n1079\t    CI, BH correction, and random-split control, this creates an airtight significance\n1080\t    case.\n1081\t\n1082\t    '\n1083\t- name: odds_ratio_regression_transparency\n1084\t  plan_id: plan_030\n1085\t  description: 'Supplement pseudo R²=0.0007 with odds ratios, CIs, McFadden/Nagelkerke\n1086\t    R², deviance ratios. Item-level vs domain-level accuracy change models. Detect\n1087\t    Simpson''s paradox.\n1088\t\n1089\t    '\n1090\t  expected_results:\n1091\t    model1_domain_delta:\n1092\t      mcfadden_r2: 0.0007\n1093\t      nagelkerke_r2: 0.0012\n1094\t      subject_acc_delta_or_per_010: 1.55\n1095\t      subject_acc_delta_ci_per_010:\n1096\t      - 1.19\n1097\t      - 2.03\n1098\t      interpretation: 'Domain-level accuracy improvement has a statistically significant\n1099\t        but practically negligible association with DIF classification.\n1100\t\n1101\t        '\n1102\t    model2_domain_plus_item_props:\n1103\t      mcfadden_r2: 0.0423\n1104\t      nagelkerke_r2: 0.072\n1105\t      subject_acc_delta_or_per_010: 0.73\n1106\t      ctt_difficulty_or_per_010: 0.78\n1107\t      ctt_discrimination_or_per_010: 1.51\n1108\t    model3_item_delta:\n1109\t      mcfadden_r2: 0.0012\n1110\t      nagelkerke_r2: 0.0021\n1111\t      item_acc_change_or_per_010: 1.08\n1112\t      item_acc_change_ci:\n1113\t      - 1.51\n1114\t      - 2.96\n1115\t    model4_item_delta_plus_props:\n1116\t      mcfadden_r2: 0.0434\n1117\t      nagelkerke_r2: 0.0737\n1118\t      item_acc_change_or_per_010: 0.92\n1119\t      ctt_discrimination_or_per_010: 1.54\n1120\t    simpsons_paradox:\n1121\t      confirmed: true\n1122\t      direction: 'Domain accuracy improvement predicts DIF marginally (OR=1.55), but\n1123\t        REVERSES when item properties are included (OR=0.73). Item discrimination\n1124\t        is the true predictor (OR=1.51-1.54).\n1125\t\n1126\t        '\n1127\t    lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2: 647.0\n1128\t    lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2: 655.5\n1129\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，Simpson's paradox是confound elimination narrative的statistical\\\n1130\t    \\ highlight。理由： (1) McFadden R²=0.0007 (Model 1) 直接回答\\\"is 31% just because models\\\n1131\t    \\ got better?\\\"——\\n    No, domain improvement explains <0.1% of DIF variance；\\n\\\n1132\t    (2) Simpson's paradox (OR从1.55→0.73 when item properties added) 提供更nuanced story：\\n\\\n1133\t    \\    domain improvement的marginal association是Simpson's artifact——once you control\\\n1134\t    \\ for\\n    item difficulty and discrimination, the association REVERSES；\\n(3)\\\n1135\t    \\ Item discrimination (OR=1.51-1.54 across models)是true predictor——\\n    high-discrimination\\\n1136\t    \\ items更容易show DIF，这是psychometrically expected\\n    (more discriminating items\\\n1137\t    \\ are more sensitive to group differences)；\\n(4) Model 4 (R²=0.074)仍然只解释7.4%——even\\\n1138\t    \\ the best model leaves 92.6% of DIF\\n    variance unexplained by item properties\\\n1139\t    \\ and accuracy changes；\\n(5) Best档reviewers视Simpson's paradox as elegant demonstration\\\n1140\t    \\ that naive\\n    confound concern (domain improvement → DIF) is misleading。\\n\"\n1141\t  tables:\n1142\t  - title: 'Table 7: Logistic Regression Models — DIF Flag Prediction'\n1143\t    columns:\n1144\t    - Model\n1145\t    - Predictors\n1146\t    - McFadden_R2\n1147\t    - Key_OR\n1148\t    - Key_CI\n1149\t    - LR_test_p\n1150\t    rows:\n1151\t    - - M1\n1152\t      - Domain Δacc\n1153\t      - 0.0007\n1154\t      - 1.55/0.1\n1155\t      - '[1.19, 2.03]'\n1156\t      - --\n1157\t    - - M2\n1158\t      - Domain Δacc + difficulty + discrimination\n1159\t      - 0.0423\n1160\t      - 0.73/0.1\n1161\t      - '[0.55, 0.97]'\n1162\t      - <0.001\n1163\t    - - M3\n1164\t      - Item Δacc\n1165\t      - 0.0012\n1166\t      - 1.08/0.1\n1167\t      - '[1.51, 2.96]†'\n1168\t      - --\n1169\t    - - M4\n1170\t      - Item Δacc + difficulty + discrimination\n1171\t      - 0.0434\n1172\t      - 0.92/0.1\n1173\t      - '[0.69, 1.22]'\n1174\t      - <0.001\n1175\t  - title: '† Note: CI for raw OR, not per-0.1 unit'\n1176\t  figures_description:\n1177\t  - 'Fig 7: Simpson''s paradox illustration — two panels showing domain accuracy delta\n1178\t    coefficient flipping sign from M1 (+) to M2 (−) when item properties are added.\n1179\t    Forest plot of ORs with CIs.'\n1180\t  analysis: 'Load-bearing for confound elimination. In best tier, Simpson''s paradox\n1181\t    is a memorable finding that reviewers cite in their assessment. The reversal from\n1182\t    OR=1.55 to OR=0.73 is the quantitative nail in the \"ability confound\" coffin,\n1183\t    complementing plan_027''s matching-based approach.\n1184\t\n1185\t    '\n1186\t- name: irt_theta_conditioning\n1187\t  plan_id: plan_012\n1188\t  description: 'Replace CTT total-score matching with IRT θ-conditioning in MH-DIF.\n1189\t    Test whether continuous ability estimation changes DIF results.\n1190\t\n1191\t    '\n1192\t  expected_results:\n1193\t    theta_total_score_correlation: 0.9986\n1194\t    temporal_theta_qt20_fpr: 0.312\n1195\t    temporal_theta_qt20_tpr_p05: 0.876\n1196\t    ability_theta_qt20_fpr: 0.079\n1197\t    enrichment_all_variants: 0.97-1.00\n1198\t    success_criterion_met: false\n1199\t    conclusion: 'IRT θ and CTT total score are nearly identical (r=0.9986) for this\n1200\t      population. θ-conditioning does not change DIF results. This is expected: with\n1201\t      N=5,227 models and 12,508 items, total score is an excellent ability proxy.\n1202\t      IRT offers no incremental benefit.\n1203\t\n1204\t      '\n1205\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，θ-conditioning的negative result是systematic confound elimination的第4个pillar。\n1206\t    r=0.9986说明在large-N regime下CTT total score和IRT θ是functionally equivalent—— 这validates\n1207\t    MH''s simpler conditioning approach。Reviewers视为\"appropriate due diligence\" that\n1208\t    strengthens confidence in the primary MH results。temporal FPR (0.312)和 plan_001\n1209\t    (0.318)的near-identity confirms conditioning method is not the driver of high C%。\n1210\t\n1211\t    '\n1212\t  tables:\n1213\t  - title: 'Table S-IRT: IRT θ vs CTT Conditioning Comparison'\n1214\t    columns:\n1215\t    - Conditioning\n1216\t    - Temporal_FPR\n1217\t    - Temporal_TPR_p05\n1218\t    - θ-TotalScore_r\n1219\t    rows:\n1220\t    - - CTT total score (5 strata)\n1221\t      - 0.314\n1222\t      - 0.834\n1223\t      - --\n1224\t    - - IRT θ (20 quantiles)\n1225\t      - 0.312\n1226\t      - 0.876\n1227\t      - 0.9986\n1228\t    - - IRT θ (10 quantiles)\n1229\t      - 0.312\n1230\t      - 0.876\n1231\t      - 0.9986\n1232\t  figures_description: []\n1233\t  analysis: 'Negative result supporting confound elimination. In best tier, this is\n1234\t    one sentence in the robustness section: \"IRT θ-conditioning (r=0.9986 with total\n1235\t    score) yields identical results.\"\n1236\t\n1237\t    '\n1238\t- name: q3_local_independence\n1239\t  plan_id: plan_013\n1240\t  description: 'Yen''s Q3 statistic for local independence. Within-subject vs cross-subject\n1241\t    residual correlations. Identify locally dependent item pairs.\n1242\t\n1243\t    '\n1244\t  expected_results:\n1245\t    within_subject_mean_q3: 0.0086\n1246\t    cross_subject_mean_q3: 0.0031\n1247\t    within_subject_pct_above_020: 11.3\n1248\t    cross_subject_pct_above_020: 2.2\n1249\t    mann_whitney_p: 2.29e-09\n1250\t    worst_subject: moral_scenarios\n1251\t    worst_subject_pct_above_020: 34.2\n1252\t    n_items_filtered: 257\n1253\t    conclusion: 'Local dependence is modest within subjects (mean Q3=0.009, 11.3%\n1254\t      above 0.20) and minimal across subjects (2.2%). Removing 257 high-Q3 items has\n1255\t      negligible impact on DIF results. Local dependence is not a confound.\n1256\t\n1257\t      '\n1258\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，Q3 analysis是confound elimination的第3个pillar。理由： mean Q3=0.009远低于conventional\n1259\t    concern threshold (0.20)，even worst subject (moral_scenarios 34.2% above 0.20)的local\n1260\t    dependence被shown to not drive DIF (removing 257 items changes C% by <0.5pp)。Mann-Whitney\n1261\t    p=2.29e-09 confirms within-subject Q3 > cross-subject Q3 (expected from subject\n1262\t    clustering)， but absolute magnitudes are small enough to not threaten MH validity。\n1263\t\n1264\t    '\n1265\t  tables: []\n1266\t  figures_description: []\n1267\t  analysis: 'Confound elimination pillar 3. In best tier, one sentence: \"Local dependence\n1268\t    is negligible (mean Q3=0.009; removing 257 high-Q3 items changes C% by <0.5pp).\"\n1269\t\n1270\t    '\n1271\t- name: within_subject_dif\n1272\t  plan_id: plan_014\n1273\t  description: 'Run DIF within 5 high-C% subjects using within-subject total score\n1274\t    as matching variable. Tests whether cross-subject matching inflates C%.\n1275\t\n1276\t    '\n1277\t  expected_results:\n1278\t    avg_within_subject_c_pct: 38.1\n1279\t    avg_cross_subject_c_pct: 40.5\n1280\t    avg_delta: -2.4\n1281\t    subjects:\n1282\t      business_ethics: 45.2\n1283\t      human_aging: 33.0\n1284\t      formal_logic: 39.5\n1285\t      professional_medicine: 31.1\n1286\t      high_school_statistics: 42.0\n1287\t    decision_zone: '>25% HIGH'\n1288\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，within-subject C%=38.1%实际上HIGHER than temporal cross-subject\n1289\t    31.3%， 消除\"cross-subject matching inflates DIF\"的concern。Within-subject matching\n1290\t    uses only items from the SAME subject as matching variable，eliminating cross-domain\n1291\t    confounds——yet C% increases。这说明DIF is predominantly item-specific within subjects，not\n1292\t    an artifact of cross-subject ability mixing。 38.1% vs 31.3%的差异reflects within-subject\n1293\t    matching的higher sensitivity (matching on more relevant ability proxy) at the cost\n1294\t    of matching variable contamination (which plan_016 will quantify)。\n1295\t\n1296\t    '\n1297\t  tables: []\n1298\t  figures_description: []\n1299\t  analysis: 'Supports \"DIF is item-specific\" narrative. In best tier, 38.1% within-subject\n1300\t    confirms that cross-subject matching underestimates rather than inflates DIF.\n1301\t\n1302\t    '\n1303\t- name: downstream_impact\n1304\t  plan_id: plan_017\n1305\t  description: 'Measure ranking disruption from DIF item removal. Compare DIF removal\n1306\t    vs random removal across 21 conditions (7 removal fractions × 3 metrics).\n1307\t\n1308\t    '\n1309\t  expected_results:\n1310\t    rho_full_vs_stable_all: 0.9965\n1311\t    dif_vs_random_z_mean: -14.91\n1312\t    all_21_conditions_significant: true\n1313\t    dif_more_disruptive_than_random: true\n1314\t    cross_cohort_ratio_dif: 1.0919\n1315\t    cross_cohort_ratio_stable: 0.9581\n1316\t    top_beneficiaries: phi-3, llama-3 derivatives (+700-850 ranks)\n1317\t    top_hurt: mistral merges, slerp models (-400 to -587 ranks)\n1318\t    max_rank_change: 851\n1319\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，plan_017的dual finding是Claim 4的foundation： (1) ρ=0.9965说明MMLU\\\n1320\t    \\ rankings massively redundant——31% item removal barely matters\\n    for practical\\\n1321\t    \\ model comparison（\\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\"）；\\n(2) z=-14.91 (mean across 21\\\n1322\t    \\ conditions)说明DIF items carry MORE cross-cohort signal\\n    than random items——they\\\n1323\t    \\ are NOT noise, they are genuinely informative items\\n    whose functioning changed\\\n1324\t    \\ across generations；\\n(3) Model-specific patterns (phi-3/llama-3 gain, mistral\\\n1325\t    \\ merges lose)提供\\n    actionable diagnostic insight——DIF告诉你WHICH capability dimensions\\\n1326\t    \\ shifted。\\n这个\\\"paradox\\\"（DIF items matter for understanding but not for ranking）\\\n1327\t    \\ 是paper的key conceptual insight。\\n\"\n1328\t  tables: []\n1329\t  figures_description: []\n1330\t  analysis: 'Load-bearing for Claim 4 and \"instability ≠ invalidity\" narrative. In\n1331\t    best tier, the ρ=0.997 + z=-14.91 combination is the most cited finding in reviewer\n1332\t    assessments.\n1333\t\n1334\t    '\n1335\t- name: threshold_sensitivity\n1336\t  plan_id: plan_018\n1337\t  description: 'C% at |Δ_MH| thresholds {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5}. BH FDR correction impact.\n1338\t\n1339\t    '\n1340\t  expected_results:\n1341\t    threshold_1_0_c_pct: 48.9\n1342\t    threshold_1_5_c_pct: 31.3\n1343\t    threshold_2_0_c_pct: 18.3\n1344\t    threshold_2_5_c_pct: 10.2\n1345\t    bh_q005_items_removed: 3\n1346\t    bh_impact_on_c_pct: 31.32% → 31.30%\n1347\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，threshold robustness是one-paragraph defense：\">15% holds\n1348\t    at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]; even at most conservative 2.5, 10.2% (1,278\n1349\t    items) show large DIF.\" BH removing only 3/3,918 items proves ETS dual requirement\n1350\t    (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit multiple testing\n1351\t    protection。\n1352\t\n1353\t    '\n1354\t  tables: []\n1355\t  figures_description: []\n1356\t  analysis: 'Robustness check. In best tier, threshold sensitivity is a table row,\n1357\t    not a concern.\n1358\t\n1359\t    '\n1360\t- name: item_level_decomposition\n1361\t  plan_id: plan_019\n1362\t  description: 'Decompose 31.3% C% into domain-improvement-explained vs item-specific\n1363\t    components.\n1364\t\n1365\t    '\n1366\t  expected_results:\n1367\t    domain_improvement_explained_pp: 2.4\n1368\t    domain_improvement_explained_pct: 7.6\n1369\t    pseudo_r2: 0.0007\n1370\t    item_specific_pct: 92.4\n1371\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，\"domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%) of 31.3%\n1372\t    C%\"是 confound elimination的quantitative cornerstone。R²=0.0007意味着domain-level accuracy\n1373\t    improvement is essentially uncorrelated with item-level DIF。 剩余92.4% is item-specific\n1374\t    instability not attributable to capability gains。\n1375\t\n1376\t    '\n1377\t  tables: []\n1378\t  figures_description: []\n1379\t  analysis: 'Key confound elimination result. In best tier, \"R²=0.0007\" is the single\n1380\t    most important number for defending Claim 1 against ability confound concern.\n1381\t\n1382\t    '\n1383\t- name: circularity_ablation\n1384\t  plan_id: plan_020\n1385\t  description: 'Compare DIF removal vs accuracy-gap, high-variance, high-discrimination\n1386\t    removal strategies. Test whether ranking disruption from DIF is tautological.\n1387\t\n1388\t    '\n1389\t  expected_results:\n1390\t    dif_z: -9.5\n1391\t    accuracy_gap_z: -157\n1392\t    high_variance_z: -108\n1393\t    high_discrimination_z: -16\n1394\t    dif_overlap_with_acc_gap: 0.626\n1395\t    dif_discrimination_jaccard: 0.12\n1396\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，circularity ablation是Claim 4的second pillar。DIF removal\n1397\t    (z=-9.5)是 LEAST disruptive non-random strategy——despite 62.6% item overlap with\n1398\t    accuracy-gap selection。This proves MH ability conditioning filters out raw group\n1399\t    differences， isolating genuine differential functioning。Accuracy-gap removal is\n1400\t    16× more disruptive (z=-157) because it removes items with largest raw accuracy\n1401\t    differences WITHOUT controlling for ability。Tautology concern completely refuted。\n1402\t\n1403\t    '\n1404\t  tables: []\n1405\t  figures_description: []\n1406\t  analysis: 'Tautology refutation. In best tier, \"DIF is 16× less disruptive than\n1407\t    accuracy-gap despite 62.6% item overlap\" is the cleanest proof that MH conditioning\n1408\t    works.\n1409\t\n1410\t    '\n1411\t- name: lr_nonuniform_dif\n1412\t  plan_id: plan_021\n1413\t  description: 'Logistic Regression DIF on 9 subjects. Detect non-uniform DIF. Concordance\n1414\t    with MH classifications.\n1415\t\n1416\t    '\n1417\t  expected_results:\n1418\t    mh_lr_concordance: 0.921\n1419\t    nonuniform_dif_pct_significance: 38.7\n1420\t    nonuniform_dif_pct_effect_size: 24.8\n1421\t    interpretation: MH 31% is conservative — non-uniform DIF adds ~24.8%\n1422\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，non-uniform DIF finding strengthens paper：MH''s 31% is\n1423\t    a LOWER BOUND because MH only detects uniform DIF。24.8% additional non-uniform\n1424\t    DIF (effect-size controlled) means total instability is ~56%。Reviewers accept\n1425\t    31% as conservative headline with non-uniform DIF noted as \"our estimate is an\n1426\t    undercount。\"\n1427\t\n1428\t    '\n1429\t  tables: []\n1430\t  figures_description: []\n1431\t  analysis: 'Strengthens Claim 1 by showing 31% is conservative. In best tier, this\n1432\t    converts a potential weakness (MH misses non-uniform DIF) into a strength (we\n1433\t    acknowledge it and show the undercount).\n1434\t\n1435\t    '\n1436\t- name: model_independence\n1437\t  plan_id: plan_022\n1438\t  description: 'Graduated de-duplication: cap models per family at K={1,2,5,10,20}.\n1439\t    Test whether fine-tunes/merges inflate C%.\n1440\t\n1441\t    '\n1442\t  expected_results:\n1443\t    k20_c_pct: 29.1\n1444\t    k20_random_c_pct: 30.9\n1445\t    k5_c_pct: 11.7\n1446\t    k5_random_c_pct: 16.9\n1447\t    k1_c_pct: 0.17\n1448\t    k1_underpowered: true\n1449\t    family_inflates: false\n1450\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，model independence是decisive：at every K, family-capped\n1451\t    C% ≤ random subsample C%。 Family structure does NOT inflate DIF——if anything,\n1452\t    de-duplication reduces C% slightly LESS than random subsampling。K=1 (33 families)\n1453\t    drops to 0.17% because N<80 is below MH power threshold，not because family structure\n1454\t    was the driver。 This turns \"5,227 models aren''t independent\" from reviewer concern\n1455\t    into supportive evidence。\n1456\t\n1457\t    '\n1458\t  tables: []\n1459\t  figures_description: []\n1460\t  analysis: 'Confound elimination for model non-independence. In best tier, graduated\n1461\t    de-duplication is the most thorough defense against N-inflation concern in the\n1462\t    literature.\n1463\t\n1464\t    '\n1465\t- name: item_characterization\n1466\t  plan_id: plan_023\n1467\t  description: 'Characterize DIF-C items: difficulty, discrimination, domain distribution,\n1468\t    direction × difficulty interaction.\n1469\t\n1470\t    '\n1471\t  expected_results:\n1472\t    difficulty_cohens_d: -0.247\n1473\t    discrimination_cohens_d: 0.23\n1474\t    domain_chi2_p: 0.32\n1475\t    difficulty_direction_rho: -0.597\n1476\t    hardest_decile_pct_focal_favoring: 88.7\n1477\t    easiest_decile_pct_reference_favoring: 96.2\n1478\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，item characterization提供DIF-as-diagnostic-lens的concrete\\\n1479\t    \\ content： (1) DIF items are moderately harder (d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination\\\n1480\t    \\ (d=0.230)——\\n    psychometrically expected (harder, more discriminating items\\\n1481\t    \\ are more sensitive to group differences)；\\n(2) Uniform across domains (χ² p=0.32)——DIF\\\n1482\t    \\ is not domain-specific； (3) ρ=-0.597 (difficulty × direction)是paper的most interpretable\\\n1483\t    \\ finding：\\n    hardest items favor 2024 (88.7%), easiest items favor 2023 (96.2%)——\\n\\\n1484\t    \\    \\\"capability improvement concentrates on hard items while easy item difficulty\\\n1485\t    \\ structure erodes\\\"。\\n这个finding是reviewers最likely to cite as \\\"actionable insight\\\n1486\t    \\ for benchmark maintainers\\\"。\\n\"\n1487\t  tables: []\n1488\t  figures_description: []\n1489\t  analysis: 'Diagnostic content for Claim 4. In best tier, the difficulty × direction\n1490\t    interaction (ρ=-0.597) is the most memorable finding for benchmark practitioners.\n1491\t\n1492\t    '\n1493\t- name: direct_li_comparison\n1494\t  plan_id: plan_026\n1495\t  description: 'Direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on\n1496\t    9,229 MMLU items.\n1497\t\n1498\t    '\n1499\t  expected_results:\n1500\t    enrichment: 0.964\n1501\t    jaccard: 0.206\n1502\t    phi: 0.012\n1503\t    chi2: 1.28\n1504\t    chi2_p: 0.258\n1505\t    or: 1.05\n1506\t    or_ci:\n1507\t    - 0.96\n1508\t    - 1.15\n1509\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，direct Li comparison是Claim 2 (meta-critique)的empirical\n1510\t    smoking gun： enrichment=0.964≈1.0, Jaccard=0.206 (low), χ²=1.28 (p=0.258, not\n1511\t    significant), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15] spanning 1.0。DIF flags and web-overlap labels\n1512\t    are STATISTICALLY INDEPENDENT。This is not DIF failure——it''s exactly what the\n1513\t    meta-critique predicts： web-overlap measures item exposure (exists on web), DIF\n1514\t    measures differential functioning across cohorts (behaves differently)。These are\n1515\t    orthogonal constructs。\n1516\t\n1517\t    '\n1518\t  tables: []\n1519\t  figures_description: []\n1520\t  analysis: 'Empirical foundation for Claim 2. In best tier, statistical independence\n1521\t    (p=0.258) between DIF and web-overlap is the clearest possible empirical support\n1522\t    for the meta-critique: these measure fundamentally different things.\n1523\t\n1524\t    '\n1525\t- name: temporal_ability_overlap\n1526\t  plan_id: plan_027\n1527\t  description: 'Quantify temporal cohort ability gap. 1:1 NN matching to isolate ability\n1528\t    confound. Contrast with high-ability-gap scenario (Llama-2v3).\n1529\t\n1530\t    '\n1531\t  expected_results:\n1532\t    cohens_d: -0.173\n1533\t    overlap_coefficient: 0.764\n1534\t    nn_matched_c_pct: 28.9\n1535\t    nn_matched_sd: 0.1\n1536\t    ability_confound_pp: 2.4\n1537\t    ability_confound_pct: 7.7\n1538\t    llama_d: -0.99\n1539\t    llama_matched_c_pct: 28.3\n1540\t    convergence_at_28_29: true\n1541\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，ability overlap analysis是definitive ability confound\\\n1542\t    \\ quantification： (1) d=-0.17证明temporal cohorts have small ability gap (OVL=76.4%)——\\n\\\n1543\t    \\    2023和2024 models largely overlap in ability；\\n(2) 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01)\\\n1544\t    \\ reduces C% from 31.3% to 28.9%——\\n    ability confound is exactly 2.4pp (7.7%)；\\n\\\n1545\t    (3) Llama-2v3 contrast (d=-0.99, C% drops 61.3%→28.3%) shows that when ability\\\n1546\t    \\ gap IS large，\\n    matching makes a dramatic difference——proving the method\\\n1547\t    \\ works；\\n(4) Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF——this is the \\\"\\\n1548\t    true\\\" temporal instability\\n    after removing ability confound；\\n(5) Best档reviewers视convergence\\\n1549\t    \\ at 28-29% as strongest evidence that genuine item-level\\n    instability ≈29%\\\n1550\t    \\ regardless of ability confound magnitude。\\n\"\n1551\t  tables: []\n1552\t  figures_description: []\n1553\t  analysis: 'Definitive ability confound quantification. In best tier, the convergence\n1554\t    of temporal (28.9%) and Llama (28.3%) matched analyses at ~29% is the most convincing\n1555\t    single result for genuine item-level DIF.\n1556\t\n1557\t    '\n1558\t- name: temporal_granularity\n1559\t  plan_id: plan_031\n1560\t  description: '6-month temporal window (2023-H2 vs 2024-H1) and within-2023 (H1 vs\n1561\t    H2). Cross-benchmark half-year analysis.\n1562\t\n1563\t    '\n1564\t  expected_results:\n1565\t    mmlu_half_year_c_pct: 34.35\n1566\t    mmlu_full_year_c_pct: 31.32\n1567\t    mmlu_within_2023_c_pct: 22.62\n1568\t    half_year_enrichment_vs_random: 181×\n1569\t    half_year_gt_full_year_all_benchmarks: true\n1570\t    dif_saturates_within_6mo: true\n1571\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，temporal granularity addresses \\\"temporal coarseness\\\"\\\n1572\t    \\ concern decisively： (1) 6-month window C%=34.35%实际上HIGHER than full-year 31.32%——\\n\\\n1573\t    \\    DIF saturates within 6 months, finer granularity doesn't dilute signal；\\n\\\n1574\t    (2) 181× enrichment vs random proves this is not noise； (3) half_year > full_year\\\n1575\t    \\ pattern holds across ALL benchmarks——\\n    consistent phenomenon not MMLU-specific；\\n\\\n1576\t    (4) Within-2023 C%=22.62% (supplementary, N_ref=62 borderline) shows DIF exists\\n\\\n1577\t    \\    even within single calendar year。\\n\"\n1578\t  tables: []\n1579\t  figures_description: []\n1580\t  analysis: 'Addresses temporal coarseness. In best tier, \"DIF saturates within 6\n1581\t    months\" is a concrete finding for the audit protocol: monitoring frequency ≤6\n1582\t    months is sufficient.\n1583\t\n1584\t    '\n1585\t- name: dif_cleaned_mmlu_demonstration\n1586\t  plan_id: plan_032\n1587\t  description: 'Remove 3,918 DIF-C items from MMLU. Analyze ranking changes, cohort\n1588\t    bias, model-family patterns. Compare to random removal baseline.\n1589\t\n1590\t    '\n1591\t  expected_results:\n1592\t    pct_change_ge5: 89.5\n1593\t    cohort_2024_mean_change: 73.6\n1594\t    cohort_2023_mean_change: -22.56\n1595\t    cohort_asymmetry_z: 8.5\n1596\t    random_baseline_z: <1.0 for cohort asymmetry\n1597\t    top_hurt_phi3: 258.35\n1598\t    top_benefit_mistral: -60.32\n1599\t  result_rationale: \"在best档下，DIF-cleaned demonstration是actionability concern的definitive\\\n1600\t    \\ answer： (1) 89.5% models shift ≥5 ranks证明DIF items carry cohort-specific signal——\\n\\\n1601\t    \\    not just noise removal；\\n(2) 2024 models lose 73.6 ranks on average vs 2023\\\n1602\t    \\ models gain 22.6——\\n    systematic cohort bias证明DIF items collectively favor\\\n1603\t    \\ 2024 cohort；\\n(3) z=8.5 for cohort asymmetry vs random baseline confirms this\\\n1604\t    \\ is DIF-specific，\\n    not a random removal artifact；\\n(4) phi-3 losing 258 ranks,\\\n1605\t    \\ mistral gaining 60——these are ACTIONABLE diagnostics\\n    telling benchmark\\\n1606\t    \\ maintainers exactly which models are most affected and in which direction；\\n\\\n1607\t    (5) This directly answers \\\"ρ=0.997 means DIF doesn't matter\\\"——\\n    correlation\\\n1608\t    \\ is high but SYSTEMATIC BIAS exists within that correlation。\\nBest档reviewers视这为paper's\\\n1609\t    \\ most actionable contribution，解决了Dream #7的CW1-level concern。\\n\"\n1610\t  tables: []\n1611\t  figures_description: []\n1612\t  analysis: 'Solves the actionability paradox. In best tier, this is THE result that\n1613\t    elevates the paper from \"interesting observation\" to \"actionable contribution.\"\n1614\t    z=8.5 cohort asymmetry is the single number that converts skeptics.\n1615\t\n1616\t    '\n1617\t- name: subject_dif_concentration\n1618\t  plan_id: plan_033\n1619\t  description: 'DIF distribution across 57 MMLU subjects. Domain patterns. Temporal\n1620\t    direction asymmetry (STEM vs Humanities).\n1621\t\n1622\t    '\n1623\t  expected_results:\n1624\t    all_57_have_dif: true\n1625\t    mean_c_pct: 30.6\n1626\t    sd_c_pct: 5.5\n1627\t    kruskal_wallis_p: 0.78\n1628\t    stem_pct_favor_2024: 55.4\n1629\t    humanities_pct_favor_2024: 35.6\n1630\t  result_rationale: '在best档下，subject-level analysis提供key interpretive finding： STEM\n1631\t    subjects favor 2024 models (55.4% of DIF items), Humanities favor 2023 (64.4%)。\n1632\t    这是content-level predictor of DIF direction——STEM capability improved more for\n1633\t    newer models， Humanities items'' difficulty structure eroded。This subject-level\n1634\t    asymmetry is NOT explainable by overall ability improvement (which would affect\n1635\t    all subjects equally)—— further evidence for genuine item-level, domain-specific\n1636\t    functioning changes。\n1637\t\n1638\t    '\n1639\t  tables: []\n1640\t  figures_description: []\n1641\t  analysis: Interpretive finding. In best tier, STEM-vs-Humanities asymmetry provides\n1642\t    the narrative hook for \"what DIF reveals about capability evolution across domains.\"\n1643\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e51e0195-9c84-4e56-b272-a71ad93d54d2","uuid":"474c065e-89b8-4ffc-8eb1-8295e55302db","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:57:52.385Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T141728/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '原始framing完全成立。31% C%被接受为genuine temporal instability，四条claims按原始强度提出无需hedge。\n  Permutation null (p<0.001)、6-benchmark replication (17.9-31.3%)、ability confound\n  decomposition (2.4pp/7.7%)、 DIF-cleaned demonstration (z=8.5 cohort asymmetry) 构成四重evidence\n  chain。 Systematic confound elimination叙事（architecture=99.98% decoder-only, ability\n  d=-0.17, local independence Q3=0.009, model independence C%≤random at every K, threshold\n  robustness 10-49%, multiple testing BH removes 3/3918） 被视为convincing robustness\n  backbone。Proposition 1 (ΔFPR=0) 和 DIF-cleaned MMLU demonstration 作为双重方法论+实证亮点。10→8页压缩成功，无critical\n  evidence丢失。 Reviewers平均分3.75-4.25，0-2个rebuttal issues，3-4条claims accepted without\n  caveat。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: 'Apply MH-DIF to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,219 models × 12,508\n    items). Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family\n    confound control, domain-specificity analysis, random-split sanity check.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    temporal_cohort:\n      n_ref: 1080\n      n_foc: 807\n      ets_c_pct: 31.3\n      ets_c_count: 3918\n      ets_b_pct: 23.4\n      ets_a_pct: 45.3\n      bootstrap_ci_95:\n      - 29.5\n      - 33.1\n      bootstrap_n: 1000\n    ability_cohort:\n      ets_c_pct: 2.9\n      enrichment_vs_li: 1.19\n    within_family:\n      llama2_vs_llama3_c_pct: 61.3\n      mistral_vs_mixtral_c_pct: 38.7\n      llama2v3_n_ref: 161\n      llama2v3_n_foc: 308\n    domain_specificity:\n      spearman_rho_dif_vs_acc_improvement: 0.307\n      spearman_p: 0.02\n      n_subjects: 57\n      all_subjects_have_dif: true\n      mean_subject_c_pct: 30.6\n      range_subject_c_pct:\n      - 20.7\n      - 48.4\n    proxy_validation:\n      enrichment_vs_li_temporal: 0.96\n      fpr_on_li_clean: 0.318\n      li_coverage: 0.738\n    sanity:\n      random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n      temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，31.3% C%被完全接受为genuine temporal instability。理由链： (1) Random\\\n    \\ split sanity check C%=0.18%证明MH procedure本身不inflate false positives； (2) 与Li\\\n    \\ et al. enrichment≈0.96是EXPECTED结果（web-overlap labels测量global exposure而非differential\\\n    \\ contamination），\\n    reviewers接受这是meta-critique的empirical support而非DIF failure；\\n\\\n    (3) Domain correlation ρ=0.307 (p=0.02)表面上暗示ability confound，但plan_019 item-level\\\n    \\ decomposition\\n    将证明domain improvement仅解释2.4pp/7.6%——item-specific instability是dominant\\\n    \\ signal；\\n(4) Within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3%高于temporal 31.3%，说明family-level\\\n    \\ capability gap (d≈-0.99)\\n    确实inflate DIF，但plan_027将证明temporal cohort d=-0.17时confound仅2.4pp；\\n\\\n    (5) 57个subjects全部有DIF (range 20.7-48.4%)证明instability是benchmark-wide现象，非个别subject\\\n    \\ artifact。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary — MMLU (5,219 models × 12,508 items)'\n    columns:\n    - Cohort\n    - N_ref\n    - N_foc\n    - ETS_A_pct\n    - ETS_B_pct\n    - ETS_C_pct\n    - Random_C_pct\n    - Enrichment_Li\n    rows:\n    - - Temporal 2023v2024\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 45.3\n      - 23.4\n      - 31.3\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.96\n    - - Ability Q1vQ5\n      - 2608\n      - 2608\n      - 82.1\n      - 15.0\n      - 2.9\n      - 0.15\n      - 1.19\n    - - Within-family Llama2v3\n      - 161\n      - 308\n      - 18.7\n      - 20.0\n      - 61.3\n      - --\n      - --\n  - title: 'Table 2: Domain-Level DIF Distribution (Top/Bottom 5 Subjects)'\n    columns:\n    - Subject\n    - N_items\n    - C_pct\n    - Pct_favor_2024\n    - Domain\n    rows:\n    - - business_ethics\n      - 100\n      - 48.4\n      - 38.0\n      - Social_Science\n    - - human_aging\n      - 223\n      - 41.9\n      - 34.5\n      - Other\n    - - formal_logic\n      - 126\n      - 40.4\n      - 42.1\n      - Humanities\n    - - professional_medicine\n      - 272\n      - 31.1\n      - 51.2\n      - STEM\n    - - high_school_statistics\n      - 216\n      - 42.0\n      - 55.3\n      - STEM\n    - - '...'\n      - --\n      - --\n      - --\n      - --\n    - - computer_security\n      - 100\n      - 20.7\n      - 48.1\n      - STEM\n    - - marketing\n      - 234\n      - 20.9\n      - 40.2\n      - Social_Science\n    - - management\n      - 103\n      - 21.7\n      - 43.7\n      - Social_Science\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1: Histogram of |Δ_MH| across 12,508 items with ETS A/B/C thresholds annotated.\n    Long right tail shows substantial mass beyond C threshold (|Δ_MH|≥1.5). Random-split\n    overlay (near-zero mass beyond 1.0) as visual contrast.'\n  - 'Fig 2: Subject-level C% heatmap (57 subjects) with domain grouping. Color gradient\n    20-48%. Annotation: domain means (STEM 30.9%, Humanities 31.1%, Social Science\n    31.6%) are statistically indistinguishable (KW p=0.78).'\n  analysis: 'plan_001是整个paper的load-bearing experiment。在best档下，reviewer consensus是：\n    31.3% temporal instability是empirically robust的primary finding（random split 0.18%排除procedural\n    artifact， 6-benchmark replication排除MMLU-specific artifact，permutation null p<0.001排除chance）。\n    Enrichment≈0.96被正确解读为support for Claim 2 (ground truth meta-critique)而非DIF failure。\n    Domain correlation ρ=0.307被acknowleded但item-level decomposition (R²=0.0007)消解了ecological\n    fallacy concern。 Within-family 61.3%被正确contextualized为high-ability-gap scenario\n    (d=-0.99)， 与temporal d=-0.17形成informative contrast。\n\n    '\n- name: rl_robustness_validation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 'Validate DIF robustness to reasoning-RL models (GRPO/PPO). SFT-only\n    baseline, alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO N=477), and 10-15 reasoning-RL models added to\n    focal cohort. Traditional detectors (Min-K%, ConStat) run on individual RL models.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    sft_baseline:\n      n_models: 312\n      cohort_c_pct: 30.8\n    alignment_rl_cohort:\n      n_models: 477\n      cohort_c_pct: 31.1\n      jaccard_vs_sft_baseline: 0.89\n    reasoning_rl_augmented:\n      n_rl_models_added: 13\n      total_focal_n: 820\n      cohort_c_pct: 31.2\n      jaccard_vs_baseline: 0.94\n      delta_c_pct_vs_no_rl: 0.1\n    traditional_detector_degradation:\n      min_k_auroc_on_sft: 0.72\n      min_k_auroc_on_rl: 0.51\n      constat_auroc_on_sft: 0.68\n      constat_auroc_on_rl: 0.43\n      delong_p_min_k: 0.03\n      delong_p_constat: 0.008\n    power_analysis:\n      detection_boundary_p: 0.45\n      tpr_at_p04_N80_d14: 0.31\n      tpr_at_p07_N80_d14: 0.58\n      tpr_at_p10_N80_d14: 0.68\n    bootstrap_ci_auroc_dif:\n    - 0.88\n    - 0.95\n    tost_equivalence_dif_retention: p=0.02, equivalence margin ±5%\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，N=13 reasoning-RL models被explicitly acknowledged为underpowered（Limitations\\\n    \\ §5）， 但directional evidence仍被视为informative。理由： (1) DIF是group-level method——13个RL\\\n    \\ models混入820个focal cohort后C%仅变化0.1pp，\\n    证明少量RL models不degrade detection（这是method\\\n    \\ property而非sample size claim）；\\n(2) 传统detectors在同一13个模型上AUROC下降21-25个百分点（DeLong\\\n    \\ p<0.05），\\n    提供\\\"DIF robust vs traditional fragile\\\"的directional contrast；\\n\\\n    (3) Partial exploitation power analysis给出formal detection boundary（p≈0.45），\\n\\\n    \\    这是theoretical contribution独立于sample size；\\n(4) Reviewers在best档下接受\\\"theoretically\\\n    \\ motivated + directional empirical support + acknowledged limitation\\\"\\n    的honest\\\n    \\ framing，不要求powered confirmation。\\n关键：paper不claim \\\"DIF is RL-robust\\\" as numbered\\\n    \\ contribution——它出现在systematic confound elimination narrative中作为第5个negative result（reasoning-RL\\\n    \\ doesn't degrade DIF），strength来自pattern （6 confounds tested, all negative）而非individual\\\n    \\ test power。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S-RL: DIF Stability Under Cohort Composition Variation'\n    columns:\n    - Cohort_Composition\n    - N_focal\n    - C_pct\n    - Jaccard_vs_Baseline\n    - Delta_C_pp\n    rows:\n    - - SFT-only baseline\n      - 312\n      - 30.8\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.0\n    - - + Alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO)\n      - 477\n      - 31.1\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.3\n    - - + Reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO)\n      - 820\n      - 31.2\n      - 0.94\n      - 0.1\n  - title: 'Table S-RL2: Traditional Detector Degradation on Reasoning-RL Models'\n    columns:\n    - Detector\n    - AUROC_SFT\n    - AUROC_RL\n    - Delta_AUROC\n    - DeLong_p\n    rows:\n    - - Min-K%\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.51\n      - -0.21\n      - 0.03\n    - - ConStat\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.43\n      - -0.25\n      - 0.008\n    - - DIF (group-level)\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.91\n      - -0.01\n      - 0.88\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S-RL: Detection power curve as function of exploitation rate p ∈ [0.4, 1.0]\n    at N=80, δ=1.4. Shaded region shows DIF operational zone (TPR>0.5). Vertical line\n    at p=0.45 marks detection boundary.'\n  analysis: '在best档下，plan_002定位为supplementary evidence in confound elimination narrative，\n    不是standalone claim。Reviewers接受N=13的limitation disclosure，因为： (a) DIF的group-level\n    property在理论上就不依赖于individual RL models的数量； (b) 传统detector对比提供了有意义的contrast； (c)\n    power analysis是theoretical contribution。 如果reviewer提出concern，rebuttal只需指出\"DIF\n    robustness is a group-level property, not a per-model claim — the 13 RL models\n    are added TO a cohort of 820.\"\n\n    '\n- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003a\n  description: 'Independent evaluation of ConStat-style perturbation testing on 200+\n    MMLU items. LLM paraphrasing → original vs reformulated performance → FDR-controlled\n    detection.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: not_executed_future_work\n    in_paper_role: 'ConStat/DVD AUROC numbers and Jaccard overlap with DIF flags cited\n      from literature in main text (§4.2). Direct head-to-head comparison deferred.\n\n      '\n    cited_constat_auroc: 0.62\n    cited_dif_auroc: 0.92\n    jaccard_dif_vs_constat_flags: 0.15\n    rationale_for_low_overlap: 'ConStat detects verbatim memorization (perturbation\n      sensitivity), DIF detects differential functioning across cohorts. Orthogonal\n      signals by construction.\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，plan_003a未执行不构成weakness。理由： (1) Paper已pivot from \\\"ensemble\\\n    \\ detection\\\" to \\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"——ConStat comparison\\n    不是任何numbered\\\n    \\ claim的dependency；\\n(2) Main text已增加ConStat/DVD AUROC numbers和Jaccard overlap\\\n    \\ visibility（Dream #8改进点），\\n    reviewer看到了complementary baselines的positioning；\\n\\\n    (3) Best档reviewers理解\\\"discovery paper, not methods paper\\\"的framing——\\n    head-to-head\\\n    \\ comparison属于future methods work而非本paper scope；\\n(4) Low Jaccard (0.15) 反而support\\\n    \\ meta-critique (Claim 2)：不同detectors捕捉不同signal，\\n    web-overlap ground truth不能simultaneously\\\n    \\ validate all。\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Not executed. In best tier, acknowledged as complementary baseline in\n    related work, not a missing experiment. ConStat AUROC and Jaccard numbers from\n    literature are sufficient for positioning.\n\n    '\n- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003b\n  description: 'DVD generation variance evaluation on MMLU. 10-15 open-weight models,\n    50 responses per item via temperature sampling, bimodal distribution detection.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: not_executed_future_work\n    in_paper_role: 'DVD cited alongside ConStat as complementary detector in Related\n      Work. Overlap statistics from prior literature referenced in main text.\n\n      '\n    cited_dvd_auroc_variant_contamination: 0.58\n    cited_dvd_auroc_verbatim_contamination: 0.71\n  result_rationale: '与plan_003a同理。DVD evaluation未执行不影响best档outcome。Paper scope是DIF\n    characterization， 不是detector comparison。DVD的generation variance approach检测variant\n    contamination， 与DIF的cohort-differential signal是orthogonal维度。Reviewers在best档下不expecta\n    discovery paper同时实现all possible baselines。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Not executed. DVD is positioned as a complementary approach in Related\n    Work, not as a competing method. Best tier reviewers accept this scope boundary.\n\n    '\n- name: ensemble_fusion\n  plan_id: plan_003c\n  description: 'DIF + ConStat + DVD multi-signal ensemble with calibrated thresholds,\n    majority voting, weighted fusion. Depends on plan_003a and plan_003b.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: dropped_dependencies_not_met\n    in_paper_role: Acknowledged as future direction in §5 Discussion.\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，ensemble fusion被clean地dropped为future work。理由： (1) Paper已从\\\"\\\n    detection ensemble\\\"完全pivot到\\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"——\\n    ensemble不是any claim的dependency；\\n\\\n    (2) Dependencies (plan_003a/b) 未执行，cascade drop是logical； (3) Best档reviewers不会要求discovery\\\n    \\ paper同时deliver a detection system； (4) §5 Discussion中\\\"future work: ensemble\\\n    \\ combining DIF's cohort-level signal with\\n    ConStat's perturbation signal\\\n    \\ and DVD's generation variance\\\"被视为reasonable next step。\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Cleanly dropped. Ensemble was part of original \"detection paper\" framing;\n    pivot to \"characterization paper\" removes it from scope. No reviewer concern in\n    best tier.\n\n    '\n- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 'Replicate DIF on GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models) with GSM1K contamination\n    gap as independent ground truth. Semi-synthetic validation. Temporal DIF replication.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    step1_temporal_dif:\n      n_items: 1319\n      n_ref: 1017\n      n_foc: 804\n      standard_c_pct: 18.9\n      external_c_pct: 47.4\n      sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n      standard_external_spearman: 0.926\n    step2_semi_synthetic:\n      standard_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n      external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.517\n      standard_delta_fpr: 0.0\n      external_delta_fpr: 0.0\n    step3_gsm1k_correlation:\n      n_models: 33\n      pearson_r: -0.478\n      pearson_p: 0.005\n      spearman_rho: -0.403\n      spearman_p: 0.02\n      partial_r_controlling_accuracy: -0.385\n      partial_p: 0.027\n      permutation_p: 0.014\n      direction: NEGATIVE — opposite to simple contamination hypothesis\n      cook_d_max_model: Deepseek-math-7b-rl\n      leave_one_out_r_range:\n      - -0.537\n      - -0.374\n      robust: true\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，GSM8K results serve三重purpose： (1) C%=18.9%确认temporal\\\n    \\ DIF不是MMLU-specific（plan_028将extend到6 benchmarks）； (2) Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=+0.818证明framework\\\n    \\ portability到single-domain benchmark\\n    （甚至比MMLU的+0.674更高，因为GSM8K是单一domain，matching更clean）；\\n\\\n    (3) GSM1K anti-correlation r=-0.478被DEMOTED to exploratory（N=33, CI wide [-0.71,\\\n    \\ -0.16]）——\\n    best档reviewers接受这个honest demotion，视为\\\"suggestive but not conclusive\\\"\\\n    。\\nAnti-correlation方向（DIF flags items where 2024 models do WORSE relative to ability，\\\n    \\ 与simple contamination hypothesis相反）在best档下被interpret为DIF捕捉\\\"genuine item functioning\\\n    \\ changes\\\" 而非contamination signal——这SUPPORTS pivot from detection to characterization。\\\n    \\ Robust to outlier removal (leave-one-out range stable) 消解cherry-picking concern。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 3: Cross-Benchmark DIF Replication — GSM8K'\n    columns:\n    - Analysis\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    rows:\n    - - Temporal DIF\n      - C%\n      - 18.9\n    - - Temporal DIF\n      - Random control C%\n      - 0.3\n    - - Semi-synthetic\n      - ΔTPR (p=1.0)\n      - 0.818\n    - - Semi-synthetic\n      - ΔFPR\n      - 0.0\n    - - GSM1K correlation\n      - Pearson r\n      - -0.478 (p=0.005)\n    - - GSM1K correlation\n      - N models\n      - 33\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S-GSM: GSM8K-GSM1K accuracy gap vs DIF-C item fraction (N=33 models). Negative\n    correlation with 95% CI band. Annotated: Deepseek-math-7b-rl as highest Cook''s\n    D point.'\n  analysis: 'GSM8K replication是Claim 3 (framework portability)的primary evidence和Claim\n    4的exploratory support。 在best档下，ΔTPR=+0.818被视为strong validation of semi-synthetic\n    framework。 GSM1K anti-correlation的honest demotion to exploratory被视为intellectual\n    honesty signal， strengthening reviewer trust in the paper''s overall claims.\n\n    '\n- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'Fit bifactor model (general + 57 subject-specific factors) to MMLU.\n    Select anchor items, fixed-parameter calibration for replacement items.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: killed\n    reason: 'Bifactor model fit insufficient for MMLU''s 57-subject structure. Within-subject\n      DIF (plan_014) showed C%=38.1% — even after controlling for subject-specific\n      ability, DIF remains high. Bifactor equating requires well-fitting measurement\n      model as prerequisite; MMLU''s inherent multidimensionality (57 heterogeneous\n      subjects) prevents adequate fit.\n\n      '\n    attempted_fit_metrics:\n      rmsea: '>0.08 (poor)'\n      cfi: <0.90 (poor)\n      convergence: partial — general factor loadings unstable for small subjects\n    implication: 'Regeneration/equating approach (original Claim 3) killed. Pivot:\n      DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter.\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，bifactor failure被reframed为informative negative result\\\n    \\ in the systematic confound elimination narrative。理由： (1) Bifactor failure demonstrates\\\n    \\ MMLU的inherent multidimensionality——这motivates\\n    \\\"1D IRT is fundamentally\\\n    \\ misspecified for MMLU\\\" limitation disclosure；\\n(2) 这个negative result SUPPORTS\\\n    \\ current framing：如果bifactor worked，paper就会走\\n    equating/regeneration路线；bifactor\\\n    \\ failure推动了更有insight的\\\"diagnostic lens\\\" pivot；\\n(3) Best档reviewers视pivot from\\\n    \\ regeneration to characterization为intellectual maturity，\\n    不是failure；\\n(4)\\\n    \\ Limitations §5中\\\"future multidimensional IRT work\\\"被视为honest acknowledgment\\\n    \\ of scope。\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Killed experiment. In best tier, this is part of the \"honest science\"\n    narrative: we tried equating, it didn''t work for MMLU, so we pivoted to the more\n    appropriate diagnostic framing. Reviewers appreciate the transparency.\n\n    '\n- name: item_generation_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM\n    generation with construct constraints, calibrated via student simulation.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: blocked_dependency_killed\n    reason: 'Depends on plan_005 (bifactor equating) which was killed. Without a well-fitting\n      measurement model, replacement item calibration lacks the psychometric foundation\n      for equated score equivalence.\n\n      '\n    preliminary_findings_if_attempted:\n      prompt_difficulty_correlation: 0.15-0.25\n      simulation_difficulty_correlation: 0.75-0.82\n      gap: 'Even with good difficulty estimation, without bifactor equating, replaced\n        benchmark scores are not psychometrically comparable.\n\n        '\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，plan_006 blocked是logical cascade from plan_005 failure。\n    Paper已pivot away from \"replace bad items\"到\"understand what changed\"—— item generation不在current\n    scope内。Reviewers不expect characterization paper 同时deliver item generation pipeline。§5\n    Discussion中brief mention of \"future: automated item generation calibrated via\n    student simulation\" suffices。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Blocked by dependency. In best tier, this is cleanly out of scope for\n    a characterization/discovery paper. Future work mention in Discussion is sufficient.\n\n    '\n- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Simulate cumulative Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006) across\n    4 successive benchmark administrations. Show power accumulation.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    simulation_design:\n      n_administrations: 4\n      items_per_admin: 500\n      n_ref_per_admin: 200\n      n_foc_per_admin: 200\n      delta_range:\n      - 0.8\n      - 1.6\n      prior: non-informative → informative (accumulated evidence)\n    power_trajectory:\n      admin_1_tpr_d10: 0.4\n      admin_2_tpr_d10: 0.55\n      admin_3_tpr_d10: 0.7\n      admin_4_tpr_d10: 0.78\n      admin_1_tpr_d14: 0.68\n      admin_2_tpr_d14: 0.8\n      admin_3_tpr_d14: 0.88\n      admin_4_tpr_d14: 0.93\n    fpr_all_administrations:\n    - 0.042\n    - 0.044\n    - 0.043\n    - 0.045\n    bayes_factor_accumulation:\n      admin_1_median_bf: 3.2\n      admin_3_median_bf: 28.5\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，cumulative Bayesian DIF是appendix-level simulation showing\\\n    \\ practical potential for longitudinal benchmark monitoring。理由： (1) Power从0.40→0.70\\\n    \\ (δ=1.0) across 3 administrations demonstrate evidence accumulation的value——\\n\\\n    \\    这address \\\"MH needs large effects\\\" concern by showing medium effects become\\\n    \\ detectable over time；\\n(2) FPR保持stable (<0.05) across administrations证明prior\\\n    \\ accumulation不inflate false positives； (3) 这是audit protocol (Claim 4) 的technical\\\n    \\ foundation：\\\"monitor quarterly, accumulate DIF evidence\\\"； (4) Simulation-only\\\n    \\ status被accept因为这是methodological suggestion for future adoption，\\n    不是empirical\\\n    \\ claim。\\nBest档reviewer视为\\\"nice-to-have appendix that shows the authors thought\\\n    \\ about practical deployment\\\"。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S-Bayes: Cumulative DIF Power Across Administrations'\n    columns:\n    - Admin\n    - N_accumulated\n    - TPR_d08\n    - TPR_d10\n    - TPR_d14\n    - FPR\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 400\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.4\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.042\n    - - 2\n      - 800\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.044\n    - - 3\n      - 1200\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.043\n    - - 4\n      - 1600\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.045\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S-Bayes: Power accumulation curves (TPR vs administration number) at δ={0.8,\n    1.0, 1.4, 1.6}. Horizontal dashed line at TPR=0.80 (conventional adequate power).\n    Shows medium effects crossing 0.80 by admin 2-3.'\n  analysis: 'Appendix simulation. In best tier, reviewers appreciate the forward-looking\n    methodological contribution. Key insight: medium DIF effects (δ=1.0, currently\n    TPR=0.40) become reliably detectable with 3 administrations — this makes the audit\n    protocol in Claim 4 practically viable.\n\n    '\n- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement/removal.\n    Ranking stability, score reliability, construct coverage as function of replacement\n    rate.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    progressive_removal:\n      pct_5_rho: 0.9998\n      pct_10_rho: 0.9993\n      pct_20_rho: 0.9976\n      pct_31_rho: 0.9965\n      pct_50_rho: 0.9891\n    reliability_cronbach_alpha:\n      full_12508: 0.994\n      minus_5pct: 0.993\n      minus_10pct: 0.993\n      minus_20pct: 0.991\n      minus_31pct: 0.99\n      minus_50pct: 0.985\n    construct_coverage:\n      subjects_losing_gt10pct_items_at_31pct_removal: 4\n      min_items_per_subject_after_31pct: 42\n      coverage_ratio_at_31pct: 0.96\n    theoretical_bound: 'For r-item removal from N-item benchmark with uniform discrimination,\n      ranking stability ≥ 1 - (r/N)² when items are randomly sampled. DIF-targeted\n      removal is slightly more disruptive than random (z=-9.5 vs random expectation),\n      but well within the theoretical bound.\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，graceful degradation analysis直接support \\\"instability\\\n    \\ ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative： (1) ρ=0.9965 at 31% removal证明MMLU has massive measurement\\\n    \\ redundancy——\\n    removing 3,918 items barely changes rankings；\\n(2) Cronbach\\\n    \\ α从0.994降到0.990说明reliability几乎不受影响； (3) Construct coverage 96%说明所有subjects仍有adequate\\\n    \\ item representation； (4) Theoretical bound给出formal explanation：with 12,508 items,\\\n    \\ removing 31%\\n    (≈3,900 items) 只损失(0.31)²≈9.6% of ranking precision，而actual\\\n    \\ degradation\\n    更小因为DIF items are moderate-discrimination (d=0.230 above average但不extreme)；\\n\\\n    (5) 这个result是plan_017 (downstream impact) 的complementary angle——\\n    plan_017\\\n    \\ shows DIF removal is MORE disruptive than random (signal存在),\\n    plan_008 shows\\\n    \\ even this \\\"more disruptive\\\" is still tiny (magnitude小)。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S-Degrade: Benchmark Validity Under Progressive Item Removal'\n    columns:\n    - Pct_Removed\n    - N_Remaining\n    - Spearman_rho\n    - Cronbach_alpha\n    - Coverage_ratio\n    rows:\n    - - 5\n      - 11883\n      - 0.9998\n      - 0.993\n      - 0.99\n    - - 10\n      - 11257\n      - 0.9993\n      - 0.993\n      - 0.98\n    - - 20\n      - 10006\n      - 0.9976\n      - 0.991\n      - 0.97\n    - - 31 (DIF-C)\n      - 8590\n      - 0.9965\n      - 0.99\n      - 0.96\n    - - 50\n      - 6254\n      - 0.9891\n      - 0.985\n      - 0.91\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S-Degrade: Spearman ρ vs percentage of items removed. Two curves: random\n    removal (smooth decline) and DIF-targeted removal (slightly steeper but still\n    >0.99 at 31%). Shaded region between curves shows DIF excess disruption.'\n  analysis: 'Appendix result. In best tier, this provides the quantitative backbone\n    for \"instability ≠ invalidity\" — reviewers can see that 31% item instability translates\n    to <0.4% ranking disruption (1-0.9965). The redundancy finding is itself noteworthy:\n    MMLU could lose a third of its items with negligible impact on model comparison.\n\n    '\n- name: item_focused_trees\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 'Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) with continuous release-date\n    covariate. Alternative to categorical temporal DIF. Avoids arbitrary cohort split.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_items_analyzed: 12508\n    n_models: 5219\n    tree_depth_median: 3\n    tree_split_dates:\n      most_common_first_split: 2023-09 to 2023-11\n      second_split_range: 2024-03 to 2024-05\n    ift_dif_detection_rate: 33.8\n    concordance_with_mh_c:\n      jaccard: 0.78\n      kappa: 0.74\n      mh_only_pct: 5.2\n      ift_only_pct: 7.7\n    temporal_gradient:\n      dif_magnitude_increases_with_time: true\n      linear_slope_delta_mh_per_month: 0.08\n      nonlinear_detected: true\n      inflection_point: 2023-Q4\n    advantage_over_categorical: 'IFT reveals that DIF onset concentrates in 2023-Q4,\n      suggesting a temporal boundary related to training data cutoff shifts.\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，IFT analysis是appendix robustness check confirming两个key\\\n    \\ findings： (1) Jaccard=0.78 with MH-DIF说明categorical split (2023 vs 2024)捕捉了most\\\n    \\ of the signal——\\n    MH's simplicity是justified；\\n(2) IFT发现DIF onset集中在2023-Q4（inflection\\\n    \\ point），这对应于GPT-4/Claude-2.1等\\n    major model releases时期，提供temporal DIF的concrete\\\n    \\ interpretation；\\n(3) C%=33.8% vs MH's 31.3%说明continuous approach捕捉slightly more\\\n    \\ DIF\\n    （expected：避免了arbitrary split的information loss），但差异modest；\\n(4) Nonlinear\\\n    \\ temporal gradient证明DIF不是simple linear drift而是有specific onset period，\\n    这支持\\\"\\\n    training data vintage drives item functioning changes\\\" interpretation。\\nBest档reviewer视为\\\"\\\n    nice robustness check that adds interpretive value\\\"。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S-IFT: Item-Focused Trees vs Categorical MH-DIF'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - MH-DIF\n    - IFT\n    - Agreement\n    rows:\n    - - Detection rate\n      - 31.3%\n      - 33.8%\n      - Jaccard=0.78\n    - - FPR (random split)\n      - 0.18%\n      - 0.22%\n      - --\n    - - Temporal resolution\n      - Binary 2023/2024\n      - Continuous release date\n      - --\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S-IFT: DIF magnitude (mean |Δ_MH| equivalent) vs model release month. Scatter\n    with LOESS smoother. Vertical line at 2023-Q4 inflection point. Shows DIF onset\n    concentration.'\n  analysis: 'Appendix robustness. In best tier, IFT confirms MH findings while adding\n    temporal granularity. The 2023-Q4 inflection finding is interpretively valuable\n    but kept in appendix to avoid overloading the main narrative.\n\n    '\n- name: architecture_stratified_dif\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 'DIF within decoder-only subpopulation. Test whether architecture heterogeneity\n    drives spurious DIF. IRT fit diagnostics on homogeneous subgroup.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    architecture_composition:\n      total_models: 5227\n      decoder_only: 5226\n      non_decoder: 1\n      pct_decoder_only: 99.98\n    decoder_only_dif:\n      c_pct: 31.3\n      jaccard_vs_full: 1.0\n      n_items_changed: 0\n    irt_fit:\n      rmsea_full: 0.082\n      rmsea_decoder_only: 0.082\n      note: IRT fit unchanged — misfit is due to MMLU multidimensionality (57 subjects),\n        not architecture\n    conclusion: Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue for METABENCH MMLU\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，这是confound elimination narrative中最clean的negative result。理由：\\\n    \\ (1) METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227)——removing 1 non-decoder\\\n    \\ model\\n    changes literally nothing (Jaccard=1.0, 0 items change classification)；\\n\\\n    (2) IRT fit不improve because misfit来自MMLU's 57-subject multidimensionality，\\n \\\n    \\   不是architecture heterogeneity——这被explicitly discussed in Limitations；\\n(3)\\\n    \\ 这个result turns potential reviewer concern into a non-issue in one sentence：\\n\\\n    \\    \\\"METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only; architecture stratification changes\\\n    \\ zero items.\\\"\\nBest档reviewer看到这个数字后不会再raise architecture concern。 这是systematic\\\n    \\ confound elimination的第1个pillar（architecture → ability → local dependence → IRT\\\n    \\ misfit → model independence → reasoning-RL）。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S-Arch: Architecture Composition and DIF Impact'\n    columns:\n    - Subpopulation\n    - N_models\n    - C_pct\n    - Jaccard_vs_Full\n    rows:\n    - - Full population\n      - 5227\n      - 31.3\n      - 1.0\n    - - Decoder-only\n      - 5226\n      - 31.3\n      - 1.0\n    - - Non-decoder (encoder-decoder)\n      - 1\n      - --\n      - --\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Cleanest possible confound elimination: 99.98% homogeneity means architecture\n    stratification is a one-line defense. In best tier, this is cited in §4.1 as first\n    robustness check and never questioned again.\n\n    '\n- name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 'Inject known contamination into real METABENCH response matrix. Measure\n    DIF TPR/FPR under controlled ground truth. Vary exploitation rate p ∈ [0.3, 1.0].\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    temporal_external_matching:\n      baseline_fpr: 0.314\n      tpr_p00: 0.326\n      tpr_p03: 0.548\n      tpr_p05: 0.834\n      tpr_p07: 0.99\n      tpr_p10: 1.0\n      delta_tpr_p05: 0.508\n      delta_tpr_p10: 0.674\n      fpr_stable_across_p: true\n      fpr_at_p10: 0.314\n    cross_subject_matching:\n      delta_fpr_all_subjects: 0.0\n      delta_tpr_p05_mean: 0.347\n      subjects_passing_p05: 4/5\n      proposition_1_confirmed: true\n    within_subject_matching:\n      fpr_inflation_at_p10: 0.186\n      matching_variable_contamination: true\n    dose_response:\n      monotonic: true\n      inflection_p: 0.35\n      saturation_p: 0.7\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，semi-synthetic validation是Claim 3的primary evidence。理由：\\\n    \\ (1) ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5证明DIF can detect moderate differential contamination\\n\\\n    \\    in real response matrices——这不是simulation，是real data + controlled injection；\\n\\\n    (2) Cross-subject matching ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 subjects是Proposition 1的empirical证明——\\n\\\n    \\    using total score on OTHER subjects as matching variable完全eliminates FPR\\\n    \\ inflation；\\n(3) Within-subject matching的FPR inflation (+0.186)提供informative\\\n    \\ contrast：\\n    matching variable contamination是real problem，cross-subject matching是real\\\n    \\ solution；\\n(4) Dose-response从p=0.3到p=1.0的monotonic curve证明detection power scales\\\n    \\ with\\n    contamination intensity——不是all-or-nothing；\\n(5) Baseline FPR=0.314\\\n    \\ (close to temporal C%=31.3%)说明semi-synthetic preserves\\n    real DIF structure——injection\\\n    \\ adds TO existing DIF rather than replacing it。\\nReviewer在best档下视Proposition\\\n    \\ 1 (ΔFPR=0)为methodological novelty contribution。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 4: Semi-Synthetic Validation — ΔTPR and ΔFPR by Matching Strategy'\n    columns:\n    - Matching\n    - ΔFPR\n    - ΔTPR_p03\n    - ΔTPR_p05\n    - ΔTPR_p10\n    rows:\n    - - Cross-subject (external)\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.222\n      - 0.508\n      - 0.674\n    - - Within-subject (standard)\n      - 0.186\n      - 0.134\n      - 0.298\n      - 0.302\n    - - Cross-benchmark (GSM8K)\n      - 0.0\n      - --\n      - --\n      - 0.818\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 3: Dose-response curve — ΔTPR vs exploitation rate p. Cross-subject matching\n    (blue, ΔFPR=0) vs within-subject (red, FPR inflates). Vertical dashed at p=0.5.\n    Shows cross-subject dominance across entire range.'\n  - 'Fig 4: Proposition 1 illustration — FPR remains constant at all injection levels\n    under cross-subject matching. 5-panel (one per subject) showing FPR flatline vs\n    within-subject inflation.'\n  analysis: 'Load-bearing for Claim 3. In best tier, Proposition 1 (ΔFPR=0) is viewed\n    as the paper''s most elegant methodological contribution: a simple, principled\n    solution to matching variable contamination with an algebraic proof and empirical\n    confirmation across 5 subjects and 2 benchmarks. The dose-response curve provides\n    the operational characterization.\n\n    '\n- name: multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\n  plan_id: plan_028\n  description: 'Temporal DIF on 6 benchmarks: MMLU, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag, WinoGrande,\n    TruthfulQA, GSM8K. All from METABENCH.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    benchmarks:\n      mmlu:\n        n_items: 12508\n        n_ref: 1080\n        n_foc: 807\n        c_pct: 31.3\n        random_c_pct: 0.18\n        bootstrap_ci:\n        - 29.4\n        - 38.1\n      winogrande:\n        n_items: 1267\n        n_ref: 1017\n        n_foc: 803\n        c_pct: 30.3\n        random_c_pct: 0.32\n      truthfulqa:\n        n_items: 817\n        n_ref: 1080\n        n_foc: 807\n        c_pct: 29.7\n        random_c_pct: 0.37\n      arc:\n        n_items: 1172\n        n_ref: 1080\n        n_foc: 807\n        c_pct: 26.9\n        random_c_pct: 0.6\n      gsm8k:\n        n_items: 1319\n        n_ref: 1017\n        n_foc: 804\n        c_pct: 18.9\n        random_c_pct: 0.3\n      hellaswag:\n        n_items: 10042\n        n_ref: 1080\n        n_foc: 807\n        c_pct: 17.9\n        random_c_pct: 0.28\n    cross_benchmark_summary:\n      range_c_pct: 17.9-31.3%\n      all_random_below_1pct: true\n      min_enrichment_ratio: 45\n      n_benchmarks: 6\n      mean_c_pct: 25.8\n      median_c_pct: 28.3\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，6-benchmark replication是generalizability claim的decisive\\\n    \\ evidence。理由： (1) 所有6个benchmarks显示substantial temporal DIF (17.9-31.3%)，远超random\\\n    \\ controls (<1%)； (2) Enrichment ratio ≥45×排除statistical artifact across all benchmarks；\\\n    \\ (3) Range 17.9-31.3%显示benchmark-specific variation但consistent phenomenon——\\n\\\n    \\    knowledge-intensive benchmarks (MMLU 31.3%, TruthfulQA 29.7%) 高于\\n    reasoning\\\n    \\ benchmarks (GSM8K 18.9%, HellaSwag 17.9%)，这是interpretable pattern；\\n(4) 6 benchmarks\\\n    \\ × random controls × consistent pattern构成overwhelming evidence\\n    for temporal\\\n    \\ DIF as general benchmark phenomenon而非MMLU artifact；\\n(5) Best档reviewers视6-benchmark\\\n    \\ consistency为paper的strongest empirical argument之一。 这直接address Dream #6的\\\"only\\\n    \\ MMLU + GSM8K, generalizability insufficient\\\" concern。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 5: Temporal DIF Across 6 Benchmarks'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - N_items\n    - N_ref\n    - N_foc\n    - C_pct\n    - Random_C_pct\n    - Enrichment\n    rows:\n    - - MMLU\n      - 12508\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 31.3\n      - 0.18\n      - 174×\n    - - WinoGrande\n      - 1267\n      - 1017\n      - 803\n      - 30.3\n      - 0.32\n      - 95×\n    - - TruthfulQA\n      - 817\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 29.7\n      - 0.37\n      - 80×\n    - - ARC-Challenge\n      - 1172\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 26.9\n      - 0.6\n      - 45×\n    - - GSM8K\n      - 1319\n      - 1017\n      - 804\n      - 18.9\n      - 0.3\n      - 63×\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - 10042\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 17.9\n      - 0.28\n      - 64×\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 5: Bar chart of C% across 6 benchmarks (descending) with random control overlay\n    (<1% barely visible). Error bars from bootstrap CI. Demonstrates generalizability\n    of temporal DIF phenomenon.'\n  analysis: 'Load-bearing for generalizability. In best tier, 6-benchmark consistency\n    is the single strongest defense against \"MMLU-specific artifact\" reviewer concern.\n    The knowledge-intensive > reasoning pattern adds interpretive value.\n\n    '\n- name: permutation_null_c_rate\n  plan_id: plan_029\n  description: '1000× permutation test: randomly reassign 2023/2024 labels (preserving\n    N_ref=1080, N_foc=807), run MH-DIF each time. Establish null distribution for\n    C%.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_permutations: 1000\n    null_distribution:\n      mean_c_pct: 0.22\n      sd_c_pct: 0.05\n      max_c_pct: 0.41\n      min_c_pct: 0.08\n      q95_c_pct: 0.31\n      q99_c_pct: 0.36\n    observed_c_pct: 31.3\n    z_score: 622.0\n    p_value: <0.001 (observed never reached in 1000 permutations)\n    enrichment_vs_null_mean: 142.3\n    null_shape: approximately normal, centered near random-split control\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，permutation null是\\\"is 31% above chance?\\\"的definitive\\\n    \\ answer。理由： (1) Null mean C%=0.22%几乎identical to within-cohort random split C%=0.18%——\\n\\\n    \\    这validates random split as adequate null proxy，同时提供formal permutation-based\\\n    \\ confirmation；\\n(2) Observed 31.3% never appears in 1000 permutations (max null=0.41%)——\\n\\\n    \\    z=622是absurdly significant，p<0.001 is conservative understatement；\\n(3) Null\\\n    \\ distribution shape (normal, sd=0.05%) shows temporal label assignment\\n    matters\\\n    \\ enormously——C% drops 150× when temporal structure is destroyed；\\n(4) 这消除last\\\n    \\ remaining \\\"statistical artifact\\\" concern：31% is not chance，\\n    not multiple\\\n    \\ testing artifact (BH removes 3/3918), not procedural artifact\\n    (random split\\\n    \\ 0.18%), and not temporal label artifact (permutation null 0.22%)；\\n(5) Best档reviewers视permutation\\\n    \\ test为gold-standard significance evidence，\\n    与bootstrap CI (29.5-33.1%)一起provide\\\n    \\ complete uncertainty quantification。\\n关键insight：null mean (0.22%)和random split\\\n    \\ (0.18%)的consistency说明MH procedure itself has near-zero false positive rate——observed\\\n    \\ C% is almost entirely signal。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 6: Permutation Null Distribution vs Observed C%'\n    columns:\n    - Statistic\n    - Value\n    rows:\n    - - Observed C%\n      - 31.3\n    - - Permutation null mean\n      - 0.22\n    - - Permutation null SD\n      - 0.05\n    - - Permutation null max (N=1000)\n      - 0.41\n    - - z-score\n      - 622.0\n    - - p-value\n      - <0.001\n    - - Random-split control (within-cohort)\n      - 0.18\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 6: Permutation null distribution (histogram, 1000 draws) centered at 0.22%\n    with observed 31.3% as vertical red line far off the right edge. Inset: zoomed\n    view of null distribution showing tight concentration around 0.2%. Visual demonstrates\n    observed C% is not remotely consistent with null.'\n  analysis: 'Load-bearing for statistical credibility. In best tier, the permutation\n    test is the capstone of the \"not an artifact\" argument chain. z=622 is so extreme\n    that no reviewer can question statistical significance. Combined with bootstrap\n    CI, BH correction, and random-split control, this creates an airtight significance\n    case.\n\n    '\n- name: odds_ratio_regression_transparency\n  plan_id: plan_030\n  description: 'Supplement pseudo R²=0.0007 with odds ratios, CIs, McFadden/Nagelkerke\n    R², deviance ratios. Item-level vs domain-level accuracy change models. Detect\n    Simpson''s paradox.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model1_domain_delta:\n      mcfadden_r2: 0.0007\n      nagelkerke_r2: 0.0012\n      subject_acc_delta_or_per_010: 1.55\n      subject_acc_delta_ci_per_010:\n      - 1.19\n      - 2.03\n      interpretation: 'Domain-level accuracy improvement has a statistically significant\n        but practically negligible association with DIF classification.\n\n        '\n    model2_domain_plus_item_props:\n      mcfadden_r2: 0.0423\n      nagelkerke_r2: 0.072\n      subject_acc_delta_or_per_010: 0.73\n      ctt_difficulty_or_per_010: 0.78\n      ctt_discrimination_or_per_010: 1.51\n    model3_item_delta:\n      mcfadden_r2: 0.0012\n      nagelkerke_r2: 0.0021\n      item_acc_change_or_per_010: 1.08\n      item_acc_change_ci:\n      - 1.51\n      - 2.96\n    model4_item_delta_plus_props:\n      mcfadden_r2: 0.0434\n      nagelkerke_r2: 0.0737\n      item_acc_change_or_per_010: 0.92\n      ctt_discrimination_or_per_010: 1.54\n    simpsons_paradox:\n      confirmed: true\n      direction: 'Domain accuracy improvement predicts DIF marginally (OR=1.55), but\n        REVERSES when item properties are included (OR=0.73). Item discrimination\n        is the true predictor (OR=1.51-1.54).\n\n        '\n    lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2: 647.0\n    lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2: 655.5\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，Simpson's paradox是confound elimination narrative的statistical\\\n    \\ highlight。理由： (1) McFadden R²=0.0007 (Model 1) 直接回答\\\"is 31% just because models\\\n    \\ got better?\\\"——\\n    No, domain improvement explains <0.1% of DIF variance；\\n\\\n    (2) Simpson's paradox (OR从1.55→0.73 when item properties added) 提供更nuanced story：\\n\\\n    \\    domain improvement的marginal association是Simpson's artifact——once you control\\\n    \\ for\\n    item difficulty and discrimination, the association REVERSES；\\n(3)\\\n    \\ Item discrimination (OR=1.51-1.54 across models)是true predictor——\\n    high-discrimination\\\n    \\ items更容易show DIF，这是psychometrically expected\\n    (more discriminating items\\\n    \\ are more sensitive to group differences)；\\n(4) Model 4 (R²=0.074)仍然只解释7.4%——even\\\n    \\ the best model leaves 92.6% of DIF\\n    variance unexplained by item properties\\\n    \\ and accuracy changes；\\n(5) Best档reviewers视Simpson's paradox as elegant demonstration\\\n    \\ that naive\\n    confound concern (domain improvement → DIF) is misleading。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 7: Logistic Regression Models — DIF Flag Prediction'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Predictors\n    - McFadden_R2\n    - Key_OR\n    - Key_CI\n    - LR_test_p\n    rows:\n    - - M1\n      - Domain Δacc\n      - 0.0007\n      - 1.55/0.1\n      - '[1.19, 2.03]'\n      - --\n    - - M2\n      - Domain Δacc + difficulty + discrimination\n      - 0.0423\n      - 0.73/0.1\n      - '[0.55, 0.97]'\n      - <0.001\n    - - M3\n      - Item Δacc\n      - 0.0012\n      - 1.08/0.1\n      - '[1.51, 2.96]†'\n      - --\n    - - M4\n      - Item Δacc + difficulty + discrimination\n      - 0.0434\n      - 0.92/0.1\n      - '[0.69, 1.22]'\n      - <0.001\n  - title: '† Note: CI for raw OR, not per-0.1 unit'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 7: Simpson''s paradox illustration — two panels showing domain accuracy delta\n    coefficient flipping sign from M1 (+) to M2 (−) when item properties are added.\n    Forest plot of ORs with CIs.'\n  analysis: 'Load-bearing for confound elimination. In best tier, Simpson''s paradox\n    is a memorable finding that reviewers cite in their assessment. The reversal from\n    OR=1.55 to OR=0.73 is the quantitative nail in the \"ability confound\" coffin,\n    complementing plan_027''s matching-based approach.\n\n    '\n- name: irt_theta_conditioning\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 'Replace CTT total-score matching with IRT θ-conditioning in MH-DIF.\n    Test whether continuous ability estimation changes DIF results.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    theta_total_score_correlation: 0.9986\n    temporal_theta_qt20_fpr: 0.312\n    temporal_theta_qt20_tpr_p05: 0.876\n    ability_theta_qt20_fpr: 0.079\n    enrichment_all_variants: 0.97-1.00\n    success_criterion_met: false\n    conclusion: 'IRT θ and CTT total score are nearly identical (r=0.9986) for this\n      population. θ-conditioning does not change DIF results. This is expected: with\n      N=5,227 models and 12,508 items, total score is an excellent ability proxy.\n      IRT offers no incremental benefit.\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，θ-conditioning的negative result是systematic confound elimination的第4个pillar。\n    r=0.9986说明在large-N regime下CTT total score和IRT θ是functionally equivalent—— 这validates\n    MH''s simpler conditioning approach。Reviewers视为\"appropriate due diligence\" that\n    strengthens confidence in the primary MH results。temporal FPR (0.312)和 plan_001\n    (0.318)的near-identity confirms conditioning method is not the driver of high C%。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S-IRT: IRT θ vs CTT Conditioning Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Conditioning\n    - Temporal_FPR\n    - Temporal_TPR_p05\n    - θ-TotalScore_r\n    rows:\n    - - CTT total score (5 strata)\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.834\n      - --\n    - - IRT θ (20 quantiles)\n      - 0.312\n      - 0.876\n      - 0.9986\n    - - IRT θ (10 quantiles)\n      - 0.312\n      - 0.876\n      - 0.9986\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Negative result supporting confound elimination. In best tier, this is\n    one sentence in the robustness section: \"IRT θ-conditioning (r=0.9986 with total\n    score) yields identical results.\"\n\n    '\n- name: q3_local_independence\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 'Yen''s Q3 statistic for local independence. Within-subject vs cross-subject\n    residual correlations. Identify locally dependent item pairs.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    within_subject_mean_q3: 0.0086\n    cross_subject_mean_q3: 0.0031\n    within_subject_pct_above_020: 11.3\n    cross_subject_pct_above_020: 2.2\n    mann_whitney_p: 2.29e-09\n    worst_subject: moral_scenarios\n    worst_subject_pct_above_020: 34.2\n    n_items_filtered: 257\n    conclusion: 'Local dependence is modest within subjects (mean Q3=0.009, 11.3%\n      above 0.20) and minimal across subjects (2.2%). Removing 257 high-Q3 items has\n      negligible impact on DIF results. Local dependence is not a confound.\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，Q3 analysis是confound elimination的第3个pillar。理由： mean Q3=0.009远低于conventional\n    concern threshold (0.20)，even worst subject (moral_scenarios 34.2% above 0.20)的local\n    dependence被shown to not drive DIF (removing 257 items changes C% by <0.5pp)。Mann-Whitney\n    p=2.29e-09 confirms within-subject Q3 > cross-subject Q3 (expected from subject\n    clustering)， but absolute magnitudes are small enough to not threaten MH validity。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Confound elimination pillar 3. In best tier, one sentence: \"Local dependence\n    is negligible (mean Q3=0.009; removing 257 high-Q3 items changes C% by <0.5pp).\"\n\n    '\n- name: within_subject_dif\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: 'Run DIF within 5 high-C% subjects using within-subject total score\n    as matching variable. Tests whether cross-subject matching inflates C%.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    avg_within_subject_c_pct: 38.1\n    avg_cross_subject_c_pct: 40.5\n    avg_delta: -2.4\n    subjects:\n      business_ethics: 45.2\n      human_aging: 33.0\n      formal_logic: 39.5\n      professional_medicine: 31.1\n      high_school_statistics: 42.0\n    decision_zone: '>25% HIGH'\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，within-subject C%=38.1%实际上HIGHER than temporal cross-subject\n    31.3%， 消除\"cross-subject matching inflates DIF\"的concern。Within-subject matching\n    uses only items from the SAME subject as matching variable，eliminating cross-domain\n    confounds——yet C% increases。这说明DIF is predominantly item-specific within subjects，not\n    an artifact of cross-subject ability mixing。 38.1% vs 31.3%的差异reflects within-subject\n    matching的higher sensitivity (matching on more relevant ability proxy) at the cost\n    of matching variable contamination (which plan_016 will quantify)。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Supports \"DIF is item-specific\" narrative. In best tier, 38.1% within-subject\n    confirms that cross-subject matching underestimates rather than inflates DIF.\n\n    '\n- name: downstream_impact\n  plan_id: plan_017\n  description: 'Measure ranking disruption from DIF item removal. Compare DIF removal\n    vs random removal across 21 conditions (7 removal fractions × 3 metrics).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    rho_full_vs_stable_all: 0.9965\n    dif_vs_random_z_mean: -14.91\n    all_21_conditions_significant: true\n    dif_more_disruptive_than_random: true\n    cross_cohort_ratio_dif: 1.0919\n    cross_cohort_ratio_stable: 0.9581\n    top_beneficiaries: phi-3, llama-3 derivatives (+700-850 ranks)\n    top_hurt: mistral merges, slerp models (-400 to -587 ranks)\n    max_rank_change: 851\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，plan_017的dual finding是Claim 4的foundation： (1) ρ=0.9965说明MMLU\\\n    \\ rankings massively redundant——31% item removal barely matters\\n    for practical\\\n    \\ model comparison（\\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\"）；\\n(2) z=-14.91 (mean across 21\\\n    \\ conditions)说明DIF items carry MORE cross-cohort signal\\n    than random items——they\\\n    \\ are NOT noise, they are genuinely informative items\\n    whose functioning changed\\\n    \\ across generations；\\n(3) Model-specific patterns (phi-3/llama-3 gain, mistral\\\n    \\ merges lose)提供\\n    actionable diagnostic insight——DIF告诉你WHICH capability dimensions\\\n    \\ shifted。\\n这个\\\"paradox\\\"（DIF items matter for understanding but not for ranking）\\\n    \\ 是paper的key conceptual insight。\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Load-bearing for Claim 4 and \"instability ≠ invalidity\" narrative. In\n    best tier, the ρ=0.997 + z=-14.91 combination is the most cited finding in reviewer\n    assessments.\n\n    '\n- name: threshold_sensitivity\n  plan_id: plan_018\n  description: 'C% at |Δ_MH| thresholds {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5}. BH FDR correction impact.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    threshold_1_0_c_pct: 48.9\n    threshold_1_5_c_pct: 31.3\n    threshold_2_0_c_pct: 18.3\n    threshold_2_5_c_pct: 10.2\n    bh_q005_items_removed: 3\n    bh_impact_on_c_pct: 31.32% → 31.30%\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，threshold robustness是one-paragraph defense：\">15% holds\n    at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]; even at most conservative 2.5, 10.2% (1,278\n    items) show large DIF.\" BH removing only 3/3,918 items proves ETS dual requirement\n    (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit multiple testing\n    protection。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Robustness check. In best tier, threshold sensitivity is a table row,\n    not a concern.\n\n    '\n- name: item_level_decomposition\n  plan_id: plan_019\n  description: 'Decompose 31.3% C% into domain-improvement-explained vs item-specific\n    components.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    domain_improvement_explained_pp: 2.4\n    domain_improvement_explained_pct: 7.6\n    pseudo_r2: 0.0007\n    item_specific_pct: 92.4\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，\"domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%) of 31.3%\n    C%\"是 confound elimination的quantitative cornerstone。R²=0.0007意味着domain-level accuracy\n    improvement is essentially uncorrelated with item-level DIF。 剩余92.4% is item-specific\n    instability not attributable to capability gains。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Key confound elimination result. In best tier, \"R²=0.0007\" is the single\n    most important number for defending Claim 1 against ability confound concern.\n\n    '\n- name: circularity_ablation\n  plan_id: plan_020\n  description: 'Compare DIF removal vs accuracy-gap, high-variance, high-discrimination\n    removal strategies. Test whether ranking disruption from DIF is tautological.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dif_z: -9.5\n    accuracy_gap_z: -157\n    high_variance_z: -108\n    high_discrimination_z: -16\n    dif_overlap_with_acc_gap: 0.626\n    dif_discrimination_jaccard: 0.12\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，circularity ablation是Claim 4的second pillar。DIF removal\n    (z=-9.5)是 LEAST disruptive non-random strategy——despite 62.6% item overlap with\n    accuracy-gap selection。This proves MH ability conditioning filters out raw group\n    differences， isolating genuine differential functioning。Accuracy-gap removal is\n    16× more disruptive (z=-157) because it removes items with largest raw accuracy\n    differences WITHOUT controlling for ability。Tautology concern completely refuted。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Tautology refutation. In best tier, \"DIF is 16× less disruptive than\n    accuracy-gap despite 62.6% item overlap\" is the cleanest proof that MH conditioning\n    works.\n\n    '\n- name: lr_nonuniform_dif\n  plan_id: plan_021\n  description: 'Logistic Regression DIF on 9 subjects. Detect non-uniform DIF. Concordance\n    with MH classifications.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mh_lr_concordance: 0.921\n    nonuniform_dif_pct_significance: 38.7\n    nonuniform_dif_pct_effect_size: 24.8\n    interpretation: MH 31% is conservative — non-uniform DIF adds ~24.8%\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，non-uniform DIF finding strengthens paper：MH''s 31% is\n    a LOWER BOUND because MH only detects uniform DIF。24.8% additional non-uniform\n    DIF (effect-size controlled) means total instability is ~56%。Reviewers accept\n    31% as conservative headline with non-uniform DIF noted as \"our estimate is an\n    undercount。\"\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Strengthens Claim 1 by showing 31% is conservative. In best tier, this\n    converts a potential weakness (MH misses non-uniform DIF) into a strength (we\n    acknowledge it and show the undercount).\n\n    '\n- name: model_independence\n  plan_id: plan_022\n  description: 'Graduated de-duplication: cap models per family at K={1,2,5,10,20}.\n    Test whether fine-tunes/merges inflate C%.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    k20_c_pct: 29.1\n    k20_random_c_pct: 30.9\n    k5_c_pct: 11.7\n    k5_random_c_pct: 16.9\n    k1_c_pct: 0.17\n    k1_underpowered: true\n    family_inflates: false\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，model independence是decisive：at every K, family-capped\n    C% ≤ random subsample C%。 Family structure does NOT inflate DIF——if anything,\n    de-duplication reduces C% slightly LESS than random subsampling。K=1 (33 families)\n    drops to 0.17% because N<80 is below MH power threshold，not because family structure\n    was the driver。 This turns \"5,227 models aren''t independent\" from reviewer concern\n    into supportive evidence。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Confound elimination for model non-independence. In best tier, graduated\n    de-duplication is the most thorough defense against N-inflation concern in the\n    literature.\n\n    '\n- name: item_characterization\n  plan_id: plan_023\n  description: 'Characterize DIF-C items: difficulty, discrimination, domain distribution,\n    direction × difficulty interaction.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    difficulty_cohens_d: -0.247\n    discrimination_cohens_d: 0.23\n    domain_chi2_p: 0.32\n    difficulty_direction_rho: -0.597\n    hardest_decile_pct_focal_favoring: 88.7\n    easiest_decile_pct_reference_favoring: 96.2\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，item characterization提供DIF-as-diagnostic-lens的concrete\\\n    \\ content： (1) DIF items are moderately harder (d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination\\\n    \\ (d=0.230)——\\n    psychometrically expected (harder, more discriminating items\\\n    \\ are more sensitive to group differences)；\\n(2) Uniform across domains (χ² p=0.32)——DIF\\\n    \\ is not domain-specific； (3) ρ=-0.597 (difficulty × direction)是paper的most interpretable\\\n    \\ finding：\\n    hardest items favor 2024 (88.7%), easiest items favor 2023 (96.2%)——\\n\\\n    \\    \\\"capability improvement concentrates on hard items while easy item difficulty\\\n    \\ structure erodes\\\"。\\n这个finding是reviewers最likely to cite as \\\"actionable insight\\\n    \\ for benchmark maintainers\\\"。\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Diagnostic content for Claim 4. In best tier, the difficulty × direction\n    interaction (ρ=-0.597) is the most memorable finding for benchmark practitioners.\n\n    '\n- name: direct_li_comparison\n  plan_id: plan_026\n  description: 'Direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on\n    9,229 MMLU items.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    enrichment: 0.964\n    jaccard: 0.206\n    phi: 0.012\n    chi2: 1.28\n    chi2_p: 0.258\n    or: 1.05\n    or_ci:\n    - 0.96\n    - 1.15\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，direct Li comparison是Claim 2 (meta-critique)的empirical\n    smoking gun： enrichment=0.964≈1.0, Jaccard=0.206 (low), χ²=1.28 (p=0.258, not\n    significant), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15] spanning 1.0。DIF flags and web-overlap labels\n    are STATISTICALLY INDEPENDENT。This is not DIF failure——it''s exactly what the\n    meta-critique predicts： web-overlap measures item exposure (exists on web), DIF\n    measures differential functioning across cohorts (behaves differently)。These are\n    orthogonal constructs。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Empirical foundation for Claim 2. In best tier, statistical independence\n    (p=0.258) between DIF and web-overlap is the clearest possible empirical support\n    for the meta-critique: these measure fundamentally different things.\n\n    '\n- name: temporal_ability_overlap\n  plan_id: plan_027\n  description: 'Quantify temporal cohort ability gap. 1:1 NN matching to isolate ability\n    confound. Contrast with high-ability-gap scenario (Llama-2v3).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cohens_d: -0.173\n    overlap_coefficient: 0.764\n    nn_matched_c_pct: 28.9\n    nn_matched_sd: 0.1\n    ability_confound_pp: 2.4\n    ability_confound_pct: 7.7\n    llama_d: -0.99\n    llama_matched_c_pct: 28.3\n    convergence_at_28_29: true\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，ability overlap analysis是definitive ability confound\\\n    \\ quantification： (1) d=-0.17证明temporal cohorts have small ability gap (OVL=76.4%)——\\n\\\n    \\    2023和2024 models largely overlap in ability；\\n(2) 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01)\\\n    \\ reduces C% from 31.3% to 28.9%——\\n    ability confound is exactly 2.4pp (7.7%)；\\n\\\n    (3) Llama-2v3 contrast (d=-0.99, C% drops 61.3%→28.3%) shows that when ability\\\n    \\ gap IS large，\\n    matching makes a dramatic difference——proving the method\\\n    \\ works；\\n(4) Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF——this is the \\\"\\\n    true\\\" temporal instability\\n    after removing ability confound；\\n(5) Best档reviewers视convergence\\\n    \\ at 28-29% as strongest evidence that genuine item-level\\n    instability ≈29%\\\n    \\ regardless of ability confound magnitude。\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Definitive ability confound quantification. In best tier, the convergence\n    of temporal (28.9%) and Llama (28.3%) matched analyses at ~29% is the most convincing\n    single result for genuine item-level DIF.\n\n    '\n- name: temporal_granularity\n  plan_id: plan_031\n  description: '6-month temporal window (2023-H2 vs 2024-H1) and within-2023 (H1 vs\n    H2). Cross-benchmark half-year analysis.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mmlu_half_year_c_pct: 34.35\n    mmlu_full_year_c_pct: 31.32\n    mmlu_within_2023_c_pct: 22.62\n    half_year_enrichment_vs_random: 181×\n    half_year_gt_full_year_all_benchmarks: true\n    dif_saturates_within_6mo: true\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，temporal granularity addresses \\\"temporal coarseness\\\"\\\n    \\ concern decisively： (1) 6-month window C%=34.35%实际上HIGHER than full-year 31.32%——\\n\\\n    \\    DIF saturates within 6 months, finer granularity doesn't dilute signal；\\n\\\n    (2) 181× enrichment vs random proves this is not noise； (3) half_year > full_year\\\n    \\ pattern holds across ALL benchmarks——\\n    consistent phenomenon not MMLU-specific；\\n\\\n    (4) Within-2023 C%=22.62% (supplementary, N_ref=62 borderline) shows DIF exists\\n\\\n    \\    even within single calendar year。\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Addresses temporal coarseness. In best tier, \"DIF saturates within 6\n    months\" is a concrete finding for the audit protocol: monitoring frequency ≤6\n    months is sufficient.\n\n    '\n- name: dif_cleaned_mmlu_demonstration\n  plan_id: plan_032\n  description: 'Remove 3,918 DIF-C items from MMLU. Analyze ranking changes, cohort\n    bias, model-family patterns. Compare to random removal baseline.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pct_change_ge5: 89.5\n    cohort_2024_mean_change: 73.6\n    cohort_2023_mean_change: -22.56\n    cohort_asymmetry_z: 8.5\n    random_baseline_z: <1.0 for cohort asymmetry\n    top_hurt_phi3: 258.35\n    top_benefit_mistral: -60.32\n  result_rationale: \"在best档下，DIF-cleaned demonstration是actionability concern的definitive\\\n    \\ answer： (1) 89.5% models shift ≥5 ranks证明DIF items carry cohort-specific signal——\\n\\\n    \\    not just noise removal；\\n(2) 2024 models lose 73.6 ranks on average vs 2023\\\n    \\ models gain 22.6——\\n    systematic cohort bias证明DIF items collectively favor\\\n    \\ 2024 cohort；\\n(3) z=8.5 for cohort asymmetry vs random baseline confirms this\\\n    \\ is DIF-specific，\\n    not a random removal artifact；\\n(4) phi-3 losing 258 ranks,\\\n    \\ mistral gaining 60——these are ACTIONABLE diagnostics\\n    telling benchmark\\\n    \\ maintainers exactly which models are most affected and in which direction；\\n\\\n    (5) This directly answers \\\"ρ=0.997 means DIF doesn't matter\\\"——\\n    correlation\\\n    \\ is high but SYSTEMATIC BIAS exists within that correlation。\\nBest档reviewers视这为paper's\\\n    \\ most actionable contribution，解决了Dream #7的CW1-level concern。\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Solves the actionability paradox. In best tier, this is THE result that\n    elevates the paper from \"interesting observation\" to \"actionable contribution.\"\n    z=8.5 cohort asymmetry is the single number that converts skeptics.\n\n    '\n- name: subject_dif_concentration\n  plan_id: plan_033\n  description: 'DIF distribution across 57 MMLU subjects. Domain patterns. Temporal\n    direction asymmetry (STEM vs Humanities).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    all_57_have_dif: true\n    mean_c_pct: 30.6\n    sd_c_pct: 5.5\n    kruskal_wallis_p: 0.78\n    stem_pct_favor_2024: 55.4\n    humanities_pct_favor_2024: 35.6\n  result_rationale: '在best档下，subject-level analysis提供key interpretive finding： STEM\n    subjects favor 2024 models (55.4% of DIF items), Humanities favor 2023 (64.4%)。\n    这是content-level predictor of DIF direction——STEM capability improved more for\n    newer models， Humanities items'' difficulty structure eroded。This subject-level\n    asymmetry is NOT explainable by overall ability improvement (which would affect\n    all subjects equally)—— further evidence for genuine item-level, domain-specific\n    functioning changes。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Interpretive finding. In best tier, STEM-vs-Humanities asymmetry provides\n    the narrative hook for \"what DIF reveals about capability evolution across domains.\"\n","numLines":1643,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1643}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PLSSPmo4zLH2evoNAxsgP4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper (8 pages) and the review context YAML. Let me now dispatch the full review with 2 Reviewers following the dream-review-full dispatch template.\n\nLet me structure this properly:\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n- Full roundtable: Step 1 independent → Step 2 cross-share → Step 3 converge → Step 4 synthesize\n\nLet me first load the submit_dream_review_report tool, then dispatch the two reviewers in parallel.\n\nLet me think through the review carefully before dispatching agents.\n\n\nNow I'm examining what the paper actually covers. The work applies Mantel-Haenszel DIF analysis to METABENCH's 5,227 models and 12,508 MMLU items, revealing that 31.3% of items exhibit significant temporal DIF between 2023 and 2024 model cohorts. The paper includes systematic confound elimination, validates web-overlap labels against ground truth, develops a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching achieving zero false positive rate difference, and frames DIF as a diagnostic tool rather than a quality metric. Now I need to cross-check which experiments from the review context were actually executed and appear in the paper. Continuing through the validation checklist for the remaining experimental plans, confirming their corresponding sections and tables in the paper. I'm seeing that most of the planned experiments made it into the paper, with only a few dropped or deferred to future work. Now I need to set up the reviewer process—I'll dispatch two parallel reviewers focusing on methods and experiments for one, and novelty plus related work for the other, then bring them together for a roundtable discussion. For the first reviewer, I should focus on whether the MH-DIF methodology is correctly applied, if the semi-synthetic validation framework holds up, and whether the experimental design is sound.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46355,"cache_read_input_tokens":24148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46355},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e51e0195-9c84-4e56-b272-a71ad93d54d2","uuid":"af6c4922-0a69-4974-80b2-da94d3829c81"}
