{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018EiwAHcVqGSXpaBJ2MPmjt","type":"tool_result","content":"paper/sections/experiments.tex-67-\\label{sec:gsm8k}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/experiments.tex-68-\npaper/sections/experiments.tex:69:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/experiments.tex-70-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/experiments.tex-71-\\begin{table}[t]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/experiments.tex-72-\\centering\npaper/sections/experiments.tex:73:\\caption{Temporal DIF across six METABENCH benchmarks. C\\% = ETS~C items ($|\\Delta_{\\mathrm{MH}}| \\geq 1.5$) between 2023 and 2024 cohorts. All six show substantial instability (45--174$\\times$ above random baseline), with knowledge/reasoning benchmarks exhibiting higher C\\% than procedural ones.}\npaper/sections/experiments.tex-74-\\label{tab:cross_benchmark}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/experiments.tex-75-\\small\n--\npaper/sections/discussion.tex-5-\\label{sec:disc_temporal}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/discussion.tex-6-\npaper/sections/discussion.tex:7:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/discussion.tex-8-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/discussion.tex-9-\\subsection{Ground Truth Meta-Critique}\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/abstract.tex-1-\\begin{abstract}\npaper/sections/abstract.tex:2:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/abstract.tex-3-\\end{abstract}\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/introduction.tex-20-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/introduction.tex-21-\\begin{enumerate}\npaper/sections/introduction.tex:22:\\item \\textbf{Benchmark temporal comparability} (Claim 1): 31\\% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations under ETS~C classification; replication across all six METABENCH benchmarks yields C\\% $= 17.9$--$31.3\\%$ (45--174$\\times$ above random baselines), with knowledge/reasoning benchmarks showing higher instability than procedural ones (\\Cref{sec:temporal,sec:gsm8k}).\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper/sections/introduction.tex-23-\npaper/sections/introduction.tex-24-\\item \\textbf{Ground truth meta-critique} (Claim 2): Web-overlap contamination labels~\\citep{li2024contamination} do not provide appropriate ground truth for item-level differential detectors. Direct empirical comparison on 9,229 items shows near-independence (enrichment $= 0.964$, Jaccard $= 0.206$, $\\phi = 0.012$), exposing a validation methodology gap in the contamination detection literature (\\Cref{sec:groundtruth})."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017Ve6VeYsmSXUuKEKZ2Ge95","session_id":"e51e0195-9c84-4e56-b272-a71ad93d54d2","uuid":"9de24995-d79e-4410-809a-c4b517e73b5c","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:59:56.568Z"}
